window.OSAP_FT=window.OSAP_FT||{};window.OSAP_FT["35"]={"https://theconversation.com/nobody-cared-new-research-shows-deepfakes-are-hurting-regular-people-not-just-celebrities-296154":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:16Z","sha":"6255f95d39ff41432cfc626e714186b78e72a19507a4ab30badf54df40708c9e","read":"https://theconversation.com/nobody-cared-new-research-shows-deepfakes-are-hurting-regular-people-not-just-celebrities-296154","bytes":181124,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"‘Nobody cared’: new research shows deepfakes are hurting regular people, not just celebrities","by":[{"n":"Nicola Henry","r":"Professor of Global & Language Studies, RMIT University"},{"n":"Gemma Stevens","r":"Research Assistant, School of Global, Urban and Social Studies, RMIT University"}],"pub":"2026-11-12T00:40:40Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["In 2017, a ",["Reddit user","https://www.vice.com/en/article/gal-gadot-fake-ai-porn/"],", who went by the name “deepfakes”, shared non-consensual AI-generated videos of celebrities he’d created by “stitching” their faces onto the bodies of pornographic actors."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nearly ten years later, AI tools can generate highly realistic sexualised “deepfake” images in seconds, sometimes using just a single photograph. Often, ",["high-profile people","https://www.esafety.gov.au/industry/tech-trends-and-challenges/deepfakes"]," are targeted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Our ",["recently published research","https://doi.org/10.1080/10447318.2026.2723677"]," – involving more than 7,000 people from Australia, the United Kingdom and the United States – reveals AI-generated image-based abuse is becoming increasingly widespread. It now affects ordinary people as well as public figures."]},{"k":"h","s":["How are deepfakes made?"]},{"k":"p","s":[["AI-generated image-based sexual abuse","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/1369118X.2026.2613437"]," refers to the non-consensual creation, distribution, or threatened distribution of synthetic intimate images depicting real people. This is also known as “non-consensual sexual deepfakes”."]},{"k":"p","s":["With little technical skill required, almost anyone can create these images and almost anyone can become a target."]},{"k":"p","s":["These tools include ",["“nudify” apps","https://arxiv.org/html/2411.09751v1"]," that digitally remove clothing from photographs, as well as AI generators that create new images or manipulate existing images from text prompts or reference images."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Australia set to ban ‘nudify’ apps. How will it work?","https://theconversation.com/australia-set-to-ban-nudify-apps-how-will-it-work-264349"]]},{"k":"p","s":["These tools are accessible, easy to find and sometimes free, expanding the pool of potential victims and perpetrators, including young people."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to the ",["Australian eSafety Commissioner","https://www.esafety.gov.au/newsroom/media-releases/esafety-urges-schools-to-report-deepfakes-as-numbers-double"],", the number of reports from children involving digitally altered intimate images, including deepfakes, have more than doubled in the 18 months to June 2025 compared with the total number of reports received in the preceding seven years combined."]},{"k":"p","s":["Four in five of those reports involve girls."]},{"k":"h","s":["What our research found"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our team ",["surveyed 7,230 adults","https://doi.org/10.1080/10447318.2026.2723677"]," in Australia, the UK and the US in July 2024. We found 7% reported being victims of non-consensual sexual deepfakes, with higher rates among:"]},{"k":"li","s":["people under 35"]},{"k":"li","s":["LGBTQIA+ people"]},{"k":"li","s":["Black, Indigenous, and other people of colour"]},{"k":"li","s":["people with disabilities"]},{"k":"li","s":["men."]},{"k":"p","s":["The true prevalence is likely to be higher as many victim-survivors may never discover that images of them have been created or shared, while perpetrators may be reluctant to disclose their behaviour, even in an anonymous survey."]},{"k":"p","s":["We also found ",["3.2%","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0747563226000324"]," admitted to having created, shared or threatened to share AI-generated intimate images of someone else without their consent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perpetrators described a range of motivations, not all of which involved revenge or an explicit intention to cause harm. Some “thought it was funny”, while others wanted to “experiment with technology” or “show off” to friends and online peers."]},{"k":"p","s":["These findings suggest deepfakes can occur within peer cultures where sexualised content is used for humour, social bonding or mockery, as well as humiliation and harassment."]},{"k":"h","s":["What are the impacts?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most victim-survivors in our study reported anger, humiliation, shame, embarrassment, fear, helplessness and distress."]},{"k":"p","s":["While men were more likely to report victimisation, women were more likely to report a broader range of harms and negative emotional and social impacts. Men were more likely to find the experience funny, although these were a minority."]},{"k":"p","s":["The harms do not necessarily depend on how realistic the images appear to be. Victim-survivors can experience significant distress from losing control over how they are sexually represented. They can also experience fear others will believe the images are authentic, and the possibility of further humiliation or abuse."]},{"k":"p","s":["In our study, one participant said they felt fearful the perpetrator would “continue uploading” images and the abuse might escalate to in-person violence. Others worried sexualised material associated with their names could be discovered by prospective employers or others."]},{"k":"p","s":["Once images circulate, victims can face an exhausting “whack-a-mole” cycle of locating and reporting images, only for copies to reappear elsewhere."]},{"k":"p","s":["Some victim-survivors also described being disbelieved or having their experiences minimised, including by authorities, friends and family members because the images were considered to be “not real”."]},{"k":"p","s":["As one young woman in the UK put it: “nobody cared, believed me or listened”."]},{"k":"p","s":["A young non-binary person, also in the UK, said:"]},{"k":"p","s":["There was kind of a level of scepticism from the people I told; because it wasn’t a ‘real image’ they couldn’t really see why I was so upset and thought it was less compromising because it wasn’t actually me in the picture."]},{"k":"h","s":["Prevention and accountability"]},{"k":"p","s":["Perpetrators must be held accountable. Prevention, however, cannot be left to individuals alone."]},{"k":"p","s":["Technology companies must make their products and services safer and more resistant to misuse. This means building safeguards into AI tools to prevent abusive images being generated, making harmful content harder to find or circulate, and ensuring accessible reporting and rapid removal processes."]},{"k":"p","s":["The burden should not fall on victims to continually search for and report the material."]},{"k":"p","s":["Australia’s proposed ",["digital duty of care","https://theconversation.com/australias-digital-duty-of-care-was-just-introduced-to-parliament-so-whats-in-the-bill-294464"],", introduced into parliament last month, is an important step forwards."]},{"k":"p","s":["This would require online services, including AI image-generation services, to take reasonable steps to keep users safe. It would also give the eSafety commissioner new powers to target nudify apps and websites."]},{"k":"p","s":["Going further, Australia could consider ",["following the UK","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/crime-and-policing-act-2026-factsheets/crime-and-policing-act-2026-intimate-image-abuse-factsheet"]," in criminalising the development and supply of nudify tools."]},{"k":"p","s":["There should also be criminal offences for non-consensual sharing and creation of AI-generated intimate images in all states and territories."]},{"k":"p","s":["We also need consent-based and respectful relationships education which challenges the idea that creating sexualised images of others is harmless fun, and which works to address the gendered norms that normalise this behaviour."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Educational interventions","https://theconversation.com/mandatory-consent-education-is-a-huge-win-for-australia-but-consent-is-just-one-small-part-of-navigating-relationships-177456"]," need to also focus on fostering social connection and building healthy relationships."]},{"k":"p","s":["If this article has raised issues for you, call 1800RESPECT on 1800 737 732 or visit the eSafety Commissioner’s website for helpful online safety resources. You can also contact Lifeline crisis support on 13 11 14 or text 0477 13 11 14, Suicide Call Back Services on 1300 659 467, or Kids Helpline on 1800 55 1800 (for young people aged 5-25). If you or someone you know is in immediate danger, call the police on 000."]}],"chars":6341},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"9725206f01d82a43bfee5ffbf0106c7cc0c2fad672898f99ab90be9f1c12bb94","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia","bytes":79509,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Bolivia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-18T14:58:18+00:00","mod":"2026-09-22T16:45:15+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Chapare region of Cochabamba Department including Villa Tunari and highway routes 4 and 24 that pass through Chapare."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["State of Emergency"]},{"k":"p","s":["A State of Emergency has been declared in Bolivia, giving police and armed forces powers to remove roadblocks, disrupt protests and detain those not complying with the new measures for up to 8 hours without charge. Follow the advice of local authorities, be wary of unverified or unofficial information, stay alert and keep away from protests and roadblocks."]},{"k":"h","s":["Protests and roadblocks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not try to cross roadblocks. The situation has the potential to deteriorate without warning. Allow extra time to reach your destination and make sure you are ready to change your plans quickly if needed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Any British national who requires urgent consular assistance, should contact us by phone on +44 (0)20 7008 5000, selecting the option: ‘Consular services for British nationals’. If you are in Bolivia and using a phone with a local SIM, please call 2-2010020."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel by Road"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check ",["road status updates from the Bolivian road authority","https://transitabilidad.abc.gob.bo/mapa/"]," (available inside Bolivia only) to see which roads are blocked."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you purchase a bus ticket ‘condicionado’ it means the bus company may not be able to guarantee arrival to your destination."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],". Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Bolivia’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Bolivia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Bolivian Embassy in the UK","https://bolivianembassy.co.uk/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Bolivia, your passport should have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive and at least two blank pages."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual Citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Checks at border control"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may need to show proof of your accommodation, for example, a hotel or hostel booking and its address, at least for your first night in Bolivia."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get an entry stamp when you arrive in Bolivia, otherwise you’ll have to pay a fine when you leave."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter Bolivia overland, make sure you get your passport stamped on both sides of the border, with an exit stamp from the country you are leaving and an entry stamp on the Bolivian side."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bolivia no longer stamps passports on the border with Argentina, but you must register your exit with Argentina’s immigration authorities (in Spanish) who pass the information to Bolivian immigration."]},{"k":"p","s":["The British Embassy cannot intervene in immigration issues."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Bolivia for up to 90 days without a visa. Border officials issue 30-day stamps, but you can stay for 90 days without any new stamp."]},{"k":"p","s":["As a tourist, you get 90 days of visa-free travel in a one-year period. If you want to stay longer, check with the ",["Bolivian Embassy in the UK","https://bolivianembassy.co.uk/"]," (in Spanish) or the ",["Department of Immigration","https://migracion.gob.bo/index.php/"]," (in Spanish)."]},{"k":"p","s":["To work or study, for business travel or for other reasons, you must meet the Bolivian government’s entry requirements (in Spanish). Requirements include a police criminal record certificate from the UK, which you can get from the ",["ACRO Criminal Records Office","https://acro.police.uk/s/"],". If you need any documents from the UK, get them translated into Spanish and ",["legalised by the Legalisation Office","https://www.gov.uk/get-document-legalised"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["If only one parent or legal guardian is travelling with a child, you cannot visit Bolivia for longer than 90 days. If you stay for more than 90 days, the child will need a judicial permit to leave Bolivia with only one parent."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Bolivia, you must have a certificate to prove you’ve had a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Bolivia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/30/bolivia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Bolivia","https://www.aduana.gob.bo/aduana7/content/viajero"]," (in Spanish). You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty. You should declare through ",["Bolivia’s 250 declaration form","https://www.bing.com/ck/a?!&&p=12b180b923e5007f8fdbbcd8b267ca6f06c33b30efbe1b0caa06c551e0985ba7JmltdHM9MTc1MzY2MDgwMA&ptn=3&ver=2&hsh=4&fclid=360c5dd0-5880-67e2-0ccc-49fa59f966a1&psq=bolivia+250+form&u=a1aHR0cDovL2FuYnN3MDEuYWR1YW5hLmdvYi5ibzo3NDAxL3ZpYWplcm8vUHVibGljbzI1MC5qc3A&ntb=1"]," (link only works in Bolivia)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Bolivia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Bolivia, terrorist attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bolivia is experiencing an economic crisis and dollar shortage which has led to an increase in crime rates. Petty crime is common in central La Paz, in other popular tourist destinations, on buses and in crowded areas. Do not leave your bag or other belongings unattended. Always keep your passport, money and other valuable items in a safe place. On night buses, use a money belt under your clothes for important documents and credit cards; theft can occur when you are asleep."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminals impersonating Police Officers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Thieves can impersonate police officers. They have used fake police ID cards, uniforms and even police stations to fool victims. They may ask to check your documents and your bags and take your belongings."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should not get into an unmarked police car under any circumstances. The police cannot stop or search you on the street without a written order from a state prosecutor."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["There has been an increase in robberies from people taking taxis in Santa Cruz, La Paz and Rurrenabaque. If you use a taxi:"]},{"k":"li","s":["seek local advice and use established companies"]},{"k":"li","s":["order the taxi by phone – ‘radio taxis’ have the telephone number and the name of the taxi company on the roof"]},{"k":"li","s":["check for a sticker on the windscreen or windows – registered taxis should display one"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not get into a taxi already carrying other passengers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ignore anyone offering help at taxi stands and bus terminals and watch your belongings. Thieves work in teams to distract their victims."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Political Situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests, marches and demonstrations can occur with little prior notice. If they occur, you should move away from the area and remain in a safe place. Stay alert to developments and pay attention to instructions from local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Protestors may block roads. Do not attempt to cross blockades in a motor vehicle or on a motorbike. Recent blockades have led to fuel and fresh food shortages in some areas."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce any risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid large gatherings and protests"]},{"k":"li","s":["stay alert and monitor local media"]},{"k":"li","s":["take the advice of local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["be wary of unverified, unofficial information"]},{"k":"li","s":["allow extra time to reach your destination"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal Kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["Tourists, especially those travelling alone, are at risk of ‘express kidnapping’ in Bolivia. These are short-term, opportunistic abductions aimed at extracting cash from the victim. Victims may be held hostage for up to several days while criminals use stolen bank or credit cards."]},{"k":"p","s":["Foreign visitors are particularly vulnerable when entering Bolivia at overland border points with Peru, Chile and Argentina. If you’re travelling from the town of Copacabana to La Paz, try to use a direct bus."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been several incidents at the Cementerio General and the Sopocachi areas of La Paz."]},{"k":"p","s":["Express kidnappers sometimes impersonate police officers to target foreigners. They have used fake police ID cards, uniforms and even police stations to fool victims."]},{"k":"p","s":["The police cannot stop or search you on the street without a written order from a state prosecutor."]},{"k":"p","s":["Be aware of your surroundings and always let someone you trust know your whereabouts, especially after dark. If you are a victim of kidnapping, follow the kidnapper’s instructions."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sexual assault"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been rape and sexual assault incidents at clubs and hostels. Be cautious if you’re approached by strangers. Lock your room when you return to your hotel or hostel."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["advice for women travelling abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Prison tours"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid prison tours. They’re illegal and unsafe. There are no guarantees for your safety inside prisons."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police and immigration officials sometimes carry out ID checks. Carry copies of the photo page from your passport and the Bolivian entry stamps. Leave the original document in a safe place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal bars"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are illegal bars in Bolivia. If the police find you at one, you may be detained for questioning, particularly if drugs are found at the premises. Legal bars close at 3am."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["Bolivia is the world’s third largest producer of cocaine. There are harsh penalties for those caught trafficking or in possession of drugs. The minimum sentence is 8 years and prison conditions are very poor. Never leave luggage unattended when departing the country and avoid any contact with illegal drugs. Under Bolivian law carrying any amount of illegal drugs or substances is considered drug trafficking."]},{"k":"p","s":["All passengers on departing international flights from Bolivia will have their hold and hand baggage searched by the Police Narcotics Division, and this will include a search of your person and your bags by a sniffer dog."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Ayahuasca ceremonies"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ayahuasca is a traditional plant used in ‘spiritual cleansing’ ceremonies by indigenous communities in Bolivia, primarily in the Amazon region, but also near La Paz. At these ceremonies people consume a brew containing dimethyltryptamine (DMT), a hallucinogenic drug that is a class A substance in the UK. It is not illegal to consume this brew, but its interaction with existing medical conditions is not well understood. People have suffered serious illnesses and in some cases death after consuming it. Some Ayahuasca retreats are in remote areas, making it difficult to get medical help."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras and binoculars in remote areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be careful travelling with cameras and binoculars in remote areas, particularly in coca-growing areas such as the Chapare and the Yungas, where people can be suspicious of anyone taking photographs."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check before taking photographs of local people."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is not illegal. However, same-sex relationships are frowned on by many Bolivians, more so in the Altiplano than in Santa Cruz, where attitudes tend to be more liberal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"p","s":["Adventure activities in Bolivia include mountain biking, salt flat tours and jungle expeditions. There are no official minimum standards for tour operators. Get local advice and only use reputable companies. Check your travel insurance policy covers you for the activities you’re planning."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re mountain biking on the so-called ‘Death Road’, from La Paz to Coroico through the Yungas Valley, make sure the bikes are in good condition. Check your guide is carrying safety equipment and first-aid kit."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are regular petrol and diesel shortages across the country with long queues forming at service stations in anticipation of deliveries. Bus services between cities may be affected due to lack of fuel and there may be less available public transport in La Paz and other major cities."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Bolivia, take these fuel shortages into account. They can make long distance travel difficult and strand those traveling by car for several days while waiting for fuel deliveries, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["You’ll need to have both a ",["1949 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and your UK driving licence with you in the car to drive in Bolivia. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Road travel can be dangerous due to poor road conditions and low driving standards. Serious accidents can happen on the main tourist routes. Some of Bolivia’s main highways are paved but most roads are unpaved rough tracks."]},{"k":"p","s":["During the rainy season (November to March) there is a risk of landslides and roads can be blocked. Check ",["road status updates from the Bolivian road authority","https://transitabilidad.abc.gob.bo/mapa/"]," (in Spanish/accessible only from within Bolivia) and get local advice before you set out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Vehicles are often not well maintained. Four-wheel drive vehicles are often needed, especially during the rainy season. Broken-down vehicles with no warning lights are a frequent hazard on roads at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buses and taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Accidents involving public transport, especially long-distance buses, are common and have affected British nationals. Bus drivers drive for longer than would be permitted under UK laws."]},{"k":"p","s":["Many taxis and most bus companies do not meet UK standards and rarely have seatbelts."]},{"k":"p","s":["Safety standards for bus transportation around Bolivia vary greatly between providers. Please keep safety in mind when booking your transportation. Some bus companies which cater specifically for the tourist market, although they may be more expensive, tend to have better safety standards, including seatbelts and better trained drivers. You should research the type of bus you will be taking carefully before travelling."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road blockades"]},{"k":"p","s":["A State of Emergency was declared in Bolivia on 21 June to restrict protests and blockades. Protest groups often use road blockades as a form of protest, without warning. Avoid large crowds and demonstrations, and do not attempt to cross blockades. Blockades can disrupt public transport at very short notice. Protests or demonstrations may result in widespread road blockades, including on roads to and from airports. Check ",["road status updates from the Bolivian road authority","https://transitabilidad.abc.gob.bo/mapa/"]," (in Spanish) to see which roads are blocked."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Air travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Many of Bolivia’s airports lack safety and rescue capability. Airports outside the departmental capitals are less likely to possess fire and rescue equipment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Lake and river travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["The boat trips on Lake Titicaca offer boats that are often very basic. The same is true of boats used for river excursions in jungle areas. Check life jackets are provided."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones%22%20/t%20%22_blank"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Forest fires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Forest fires are common during the dry season (May to October) and affect some parts of Southern and Eastern Bolivia. This can impact air quality in the areas most affected by the fires but also in other parts of the country, including La Paz. It is advisable to wear a face mask if the air quality is particularly bad, or to stay inside."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding, landslides and snowfall"]},{"k":"p","s":["Floods and landslides are common, particularly in mountainous areas during the rainy season (November to March), although weather can be unpredictable throughout the year. Roads can become impassable for days at a time. Travellers may become stranded in high, remote areas. Take food, water and warm clothing with you in case of delays or bad weather."]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Earthquakes can happen in Bolivia, although serious earthquakes are rare. Many buildings, particularly older buildings and those outside major cities, may not be built to withstand earthquakes."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re affected by an earthquake:"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of local authorities"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re indoors, stay inside and take cover under a sturdy piece of furniture or against an interior wall, away from windows"]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re outdoors, move away from buildings, trees and power lines"]},{"k":"li","s":["be aware of the risk of aftershocks"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should familiarise yourself with general earthquake safety advice before travelling."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional Risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Bolivia. It only covers regions where FCDO has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia/warnings-and-insurance"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Chapare Region of Cochabamba Department"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the Chapare region of Cochabamba Department. This includes Villa Tunari and highway routes 4 and 24 that pass through Chapare. This is due to a high level of gang-related violent crime predominantly linked to the production and trafficking of illegal drugs."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is difficult for the British Embassy to provide in-person emergency or consular support in these areas. Local authorities may also be very limited in the help they can provide."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 118 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Public healthcare in Bolivia can be inconsistent in response times and quality of service throughout the country. In remote areas the provision of emergency medical assistance is limited. Consider private alternatives if they are available."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccination recommendations for Bolivia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/30/bolivia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Bolivia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/30/bolivia"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Oropouche virus disease"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zika virus"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Bolivia, including in La Paz and the Salar de Uyuni salt flats. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some medications are currently in short supply in Bolivia. If you take prescription medicine, please ensure you have enough medicine to cover your stay in Bolivia. You must bring your prescription with you."]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Bolivia"]},{"k":"p","s":["The public healthcare system does not meet the same standards as the UK, and you may not be able to access the public health system as it is already overstretched. Bolivia is also prone to shortages in medical supplies and pharmaceuticals. There are private clinics in all main cities that work with international insurance. It is very important to have travel insurance and access to funds, as you will need to pay up front to receive treatment."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Bolivia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bolivia-medical-facilities-and-practitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Bolivia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 118"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 110"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 119"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Bolivia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Bolivia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Bolivia"]," in Bolivia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Bolivia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bolivia-bereavement-packinformation"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Bolivia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bolivia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/bolivia/british-embassy-la-paz"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/bolivia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Bolivia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-bolivia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":21988,"change":"Updated information about the State of Emergency ('Warnings and insurance' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/canadas-international-student-cap-hit-atlantic-universities-hard-heres-why-it-matters-295649":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:30Z","sha":"0ab36aa7a66214ee0c03ceabee9cd268ed717bb74794df0955e3d889edae3c21","read":"https://theconversation.com/canadas-international-student-cap-hit-atlantic-universities-hard-heres-why-it-matters-295649","bytes":184287,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Canada’s international student cap hit Atlantic universities hard. Here’s why it matters","by":[{"n":"Dale Kirby","r":"Professor, Faculty of Education, Memorial University of Newfoundland"}],"pub":"2026-11-11T12:10:44Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":[["Canada’s efforts to reduce international student numbers","https://www.canada.ca/en/auditor-general/media-room/international-student-program-reforms-controlled-growth-fell-short-improving-integrity.html"]," have had a striking effect in Atlantic Canada. Universities in the region have lost nearly half their international students in three years."]},{"k":"p","s":["According to ",["preliminary figures released in October","https://atlanticuniversities.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/web_AAU-enrolment-press-release-Oct-12-FINAL-EN_FR.pdf"],", international enrolment fell by 3,020 students (18 per cent) in the past year. That brings the decline since federal restrictions began in January 2024 to almost 48 per cent."]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada’s restrictions aim to address national concerns, but their effects vary across the country. The sharp decline in Atlantic Canada raises questions about whether federal policy takes enough account of smaller provinces."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["International students cap falsely blames them for Canada’s housing and health-care woes","https://theconversation.com/international-students-cap-falsely-blames-them-for-canadas-housing-and-health-care-woes-221859"]]},{"k":"h","s":["A decline beyond expectations"]},{"k":"p","s":["In 2024, Ottawa ",["introduced a cap","https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/news/2024/01/canada-to-stabilize-growth-and-decrease-number-of-new-international-student-permits-issued-to-approximately-360000-for-2024.html"]," on international student study permit applications. The government cited rapid growth, housing pressures and concerns about oversight."]},{"k":"p","s":["The government subsequently ",["set further limits","https://www.canada.ca/en/immigration-refugees-citizenship/news/notices/2026-provincial-territorial-allocations-under-international-student-cap.html"]," on international student enrolments for 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["There were good reasons for reform. International student recruitment had grown quickly, and governments needed to ensure that institutions could support the students they admitted."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet the scale and distribution of the decline have surprised even federal officials."]},{"k":"p","s":["In March, ",["Canada’s Auditor General reported","https://www.canada.ca/en/auditor-general/our-work/audit-reports/auditor-general-report-2026-international-student-program-reforms.html"]," that the restrictions had reduced new study permit approvals more sharply than expected. Ottawa anticipated declines of no more than 10 per cent in several smaller provinces, including all four Atlantic provinces. It even expected an increase in Newfoundland and Labrador. Instead, approvals fell by at least 59 per cent in these provinces."]},{"k":"p","s":["The federal immigration department could not explain why approval rates fell so far below expectations. Allocating study permit applications to provinces does not guarantee that students will receive permits, accept university offers or enrol."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nor can the entire enrolment decline be blamed on the federal cap. Student applications, permit approval rates, financial pressures and Canada’s appeal as a study destination also affect enrolment."]},{"k":"h","s":["The scene at Memorial University"]},{"k":"p","s":["Where I work in the faculty of education at Memorial University in Newfoundland, international enrolment ",["fell from 4,889 students in 2023 to 2,682 in fall 2026","https://www.cbc.ca/news/canada/newfoundland-labrador/mun-international-students-decline-9.7389650"],", a decrease of more than 45 per cent."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are signs of improvement. New international enrolment increased by 14 per cent this fall. But rebuilding student numbers after several years of decline will take time."]},{"k":"p","s":["In ",["an October update","https://gazette.mun.ca/teaching-and-learning/enrolment-update-2"],", Memorial reported that total enrolment had fallen by two per cent over the past year. This happened despite increases in new undergraduate and graduate students. Memorial’s experience shows how changes in immigration policy can make long-term university planning more difficult."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why regional differences matter"]},{"k":"p","s":["Atlantic Canada faces circumstances that differ greatly from Canada’s large metropolitan centres."]},{"k":"p","s":["A recent ",["Atlantic Economic Panel report","https://aep-peca.ca/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/AEP-Full-Report-compressed-2.pdf"]," identifies an aging population and ongoing difficulties finding workers as barriers to economic growth. It also highlights the importance of immigration in sustaining population growth and addressing labour shortages."]},{"k":"p","s":["International students are not a substitute for sound immigration or workforce development policies. Not all international graduates choose to remain in Canada. Those who wish to stay must find suitable employment and meet immigration requirements."]},{"k":"p","s":["Nevertheless, post-secondary education can provide a pathway into the Canadian workforce. International students in Atlantic Canada can develop professional networks, gain local work experience and build careers in the region."]},{"k":"p","s":["Falling international enrolment also affects university finances. ",["Statistics Canada reports","https://www150.statcan.gc.ca/n1/daily-quotidien/250910/cg-d003-png-eng.htm"]," that international undergraduates paid an average of $41,746 in tuition in 2025–26. Canadian undergraduates paid an average of $7,734."]},{"k":"p","s":["Although fees vary by province and program, declining international enrolment can disproportionately affect university budgets. ",["It’s been estimated","https://higheredstrategy.com/the-state-of-post-secondary-education-in-canada-2026"]," that Canadian universities lost about $1 billion in annual international tuition revenue between 2023-24 and 2025-26. Further losses are projected through 2030-31."]},{"k":"p","s":["That doesn’t mean universities should depend indefinitely on international tuition to balance their budgets. Heavy reliance on one revenue source ",["leaves institutions vulnerable when policies change","https://press.insciencepress.org/index.php/press/catalog/view/38/48/744-1"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["A better way to assess the policy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Addressing the enrolment decline doesn’t mean returning to the previous approach to international student recruitment. Concerns about housing, student protection and the integrity of the study permit process are important."]},{"k":"p","s":["But reducing study permit numbers should not be the only measure of success. The federal government should examine why approval rates differ so sharply among provinces. It should also consider regional needs and whether universities can adequately support international students."]},{"k":"p","s":["Provincial governments and universities have responsibilities too. These include providing housing and student services, maintaining sound recruitment practices and helping graduates find employment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Canada identifies international students as ‘ideal immigrants’ but supports are lacking","https://theconversation.com/canada-identifies-international-students-as-ideal-immigrants-but-supports-are-lacking-191105"]]},{"k":"p","s":["Canada needs policies that balance immigration goals with the unique needs of its regions. This doesn’t mean abandoning national limits; it means examining their effects and making changes where needed."]},{"k":"p","s":["Atlantic Canada’s experience shows that reducing international student numbers is not enough to judge whether a policy works. Its impacts on universities, students and the communities they serve matter too."]}],"chars":5660},"https://theconversation.com/terpaksa-nyawit-di-tengah-karhutla-buruh-perempuan-menanggung-beban-berlapis-294942":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T16:47Z","sha":"5fab880166d39be54d1b95ec6fff58d5162a5a32c6bb6bb913573572107f2fca","read":"https://theconversation.com/terpaksa-nyawit-di-tengah-karhutla-buruh-perempuan-menanggung-beban-berlapis-294942","bytes":178803,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Terpaksa ‘nyawit’ di tengah karhutla, buruh perempuan menanggung beban berlapis","by":[{"n":"Hariati Sinaga","r":"Assistant Professor, Universitas Indonesia"}],"pub":"2026-10-28T08:29:57Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["● Buruh perempuan sawit terpaksa bekerja di tengah karhutla agar tetap mendapatkan upah."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Di tengah kepungan asap, perempuan menanggung risiko kesehatan dan biayanya secara mandiri."]},{"k":"p","s":["● Beban adaptasi bencana memperberat kerja domestik dan produktif perempuan tanpa kompensasi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ketika kebakaran hutan dan lahan (karhutla) melanda sejumlah wilayah di Indonesia, perhatian publik banyak tertuju pada kerusakan hutan, kematian satwa, dan dampak asap terhadap kesehatan masyarakat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Padahal, ada kelompok yang kerap luput dari pembahasan: buruh perkebunan sawit, terutama perempuan, yang harus tetap bekerja di tengah kepungan asap."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dari pengamatan rutin dan mendengar cerita langsung dari lima orang buruh perempuan di Kalimantan Barat, saya menemukan kenyataan miris: mereka tetap harus bekerja meskipun asap pekat."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bagi mereka, asap menciptakan dilema luar biasa. Berhenti bekerja bisa berarti kehilangan upah. Sementara itu, tetap bekerja berarti menghadapi risiko kesehatan yang belum tentu diimbangi perlindungan memadai dari perusahaan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Tetap bekerja meski asap pekat"]},{"k":"p","s":["Di perkebunan sawit, ",["buruh dengan status Syarat Kerja Utama (SKU)","https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-68944-5_9?"]," memiliki hubungan kerja yang relatif lebih tetap. Namun, mereka tetap dituntut memenuhi target. Buruh sawit SKU ini boleh cuti, tapi tidak selalu mudah digunakan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Situasi lebih sulit sebenarnya dialami buruh harian lepas (BHL) kebun sawit, yang umumnya tidak memperoleh cuti (alias libur tetap dibayar), termasuk ketika sakit. Pekerja harian inilah yang sebenarnya menjadi tulang punggung industri sawit nasional karena jumlahnya diperkirakan mencapai ",["70% dari seluruh buruh perkebunan sawit","https://www.betahita.id/berita/11823/rambo-kepada-presiden-prabowo-buruh-sawit-paling-miskin"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Sayangnya, banyak buruh perempuan bekerja di perkebunan sawit dengan ",["status BHL","https://online-journal.unja.ac.id/jseb/id/article/view/24542"],". Akibatnya, ketika memilih tidak bekerja karena asap terlalu pekat atau kondisi tubuh memburuk, mereka harus menanggung kehilangan pendapatan hari itu. Pilihannya menjadi sulit: menjaga kesehatan atau memastikan kebutuhan rumah tangga tetap terpenuhi."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dengan status BHL, buruh perempuan bergantung pada upah harian yang dihitung berdasarkan Hari Kerja (HK). ",["Studi menunjukkan bahwa buruh perempuan dengan status BHL mendapatkan upah di bawah upah minimum, bahkan tidak cukup untuk memenuhi kebutuhan hidup mereka","https://indonesianfeministjournal.org/index.php/IFJ/article/view/886/544"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian di Kapuas Hulu, Kalimantan Barat","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1389934121002884?via%3Dihub"],", menunjukkan keterlibatan perempuan dalam perkebunan sawit berkaitan dengan meningkatnya waktu kerja produktif mereka, sekaligus berkurangnya waktu untuk beristirahat, tidur, dan menikmati waktu luang. Temuan ini menunjukkan bahwa beban kerja perempuan tidak berhenti ketika jam kerja selesai."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam situasi karhutla, kerentanan tersebut menjadi semakin berat. Bagi buruh perempuan yang sedang hamil, paparan asap juga berisiko mengganggu kesehatan janin."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Penelitian mengenai kebakaran hutan Indonesia","https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC6431162/"]," menemukan hubungan antara paparan polusi udara selama masa kehamilan dan gangguan pertumbuhan anak hingga usia remaja. Temuan ini memperlihatkan bahwa dampak asap dapat berlangsung jauh setelah api padam."]},{"k":"h","s":["Masker dibeli dengan uang sendiri"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sayangnya, kewajiban bekerja saat karhutla tidak selalu disertai perlindungan memadai. Seorang buruh perempuan suatu perkebunan sawit di Kalimantan Barat bercerita kepada saya bahwa perusahaan hanya menyediakan masker pada awal terjadinya karhutla 2026. Setelah itu, ia harus membeli masker sendiri untuk melindungi diri dari asap."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pengalaman ini memperlihatkan bagaimana biaya menghadapi bencana dapat dialihkan dari perusahaan kepada buruh. Mereka tetap dituntut bekerja, tetapi harus mengeluarkan uang sendiri untuk mengurangi risiko kesehatan di tempat kerja."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam melakukan kerja perkebunan sawit sehari-hari, buruh perempuan perkebunan sawit ",["menghadapi paparan racun","https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/full/10.1080/15487733.2025.2532213#abstract"]," melalui bahan agrokimia dan air yang tercemar, yang kemudian berdampak pada kesehatan mereka. Situasi ini diperparah dengan bencana karhutla yang menimbulkan asap beracun yang dihirup oleh buruh perempuan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Kerentanan tersebut sejalan dengan ",["catatan Organisasi Perburuhan Internasional (ILO) pada 2024","https://www.ilo.org/resource/news/eliminating-vulnerability-female-workers-exploitation-palm-oil-and"],", yang menyoroti keterbatasan perlindungan keselamatan dan kesehatan kerja, jaminan sosial, serta upah yang layak bagi perempuan di sektor perkebunan sawit. Status kerja yang tidak tetap membuat akses mereka terhadap perlindungan semakin terbatas."]},{"k":"h","s":["Pekerjaan belum selesai ketika pulang"]},{"k":"p","s":["Beban buruh perempuan tidak berakhir setelah meninggalkan perkebunan. Ketika anggota keluarga jatuh sakit akibat paparan asap, perempuan sering kali menjadi pihak yang bertanggung jawab merawat mereka."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada saat yang sama, pekerjaan rumah tangga seperti memasak, membersihkan rumah, dan mengurus anak tetap harus dilakukan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Buruh perempuan juga dapat dilibatkan perusahaan dalam pekerjaan tambahan, termasuk membantu memadamkan api di area perkebunan. Pekerjaan ini menambah risiko dan beban tenaga, terutama jika tidak disertai perlindungan maupun upah tambahan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dengan demikian, ongkos karhutla bukan hanya biaya membeli masker atau pengobatan. Ada pula waktu istirahat yang hilang, pendapatan yang berkurang, dan pekerjaan perawatan yang tidak dibayar."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Riset","https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S1389934121002884?via%3Dihub"]," menunjukkan bahwa keterbatasan waktu dan berkurangnya waktu istirahat merupakan bagian penting dari dampak sosial perkebunan sawit terhadap perempuan."]},{"k":"h","s":["Perlindungan buruh tak boleh terpisah dari penanganan karhutla"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pengalaman buruh perempuan menunjukkan bahwa penanganan karhutla tidak cukup hanya berfokus pada pemadaman api dan pemulihan lingkungan. Perlindungan terhadap orang-orang yang bekerja di wilayah terdampak juga harus menjadi prioritas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Dalam beberapa kasus, perusahaan perkebunan menyediakan layanan cek kesehatan kepada para pekerjanya. Selain dapat digunakan untuk memantau kondisi kesehatan buruh perempuan, hasil cek kesehatan ini dapat menjadi dokumentasi penting tentang risiko kesehatan bawaan yang dimiliki buruh perempuan."]},{"k":"p","s":["Perusahaan perlu menyediakan masker yang sesuai dengan risiko paparan, fasilitas kesehatan, dan prosedur kerja yang mengutamakan keselamatan. Buruh juga harus memiliki perlindungan pendapatan ketika kondisi berbahaya membuat pekerjaan tidak aman dilakukan. Pemerintah perlu memastikan hak ketenagakerjaan tersebut benar-benar diterapkan, termasuk bagi buruh harian lepas."]},{"k":"p","s":["Pada saat yang sama, layanan kesehatan dan dukungan bagi keluarga terdampak perlu diperkuat agar beban perawatan tidak terus dibebankan kepada perempuan. Dalam jangka panjang, upaya mencegah kebakaran dan membatasi ekspansi perkebunan monokultur ke kawasan hutan juga penting untuk mengurangi risiko ekologis."]},{"k":"p","s":["Karhutla memang membakar lahan dan merusak ekosistem. Namun, dampaknya juga terasa dalam kehidupan sehari-hari buruh yang harus terus bekerja, mengeluarkan uang untuk melindungi diri, lalu pulang untuk merawat keluarga."]},{"k":"p","s":["Tanpa perubahan dalam perlindungan kerja dan pembagian beban perawatan, perempuan akan terus menanggung ongkos bencana yang jauh lebih besar daripada yang terlihat di balik kepulan asap."]}],"chars":6830},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/montenegro":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"bcc8f2e3384d7811ad7081f7223690fbbe5ea0b1c8f5be121a49c98528b51c50","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/montenegro","bytes":79808,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Montenegro travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-15T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-13T16:25:26+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel disruption"]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports can be very busy during the summer months, with delays possible at check-in, security screening and passport control. Arrive at the airport well in advance of your scheduled departure."]},{"k":"p","s":["For road travel you should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["monitor local media and official announcements"]},{"k":"li","s":["plan your journey in advance"]},{"k":"li","s":["allow extra time for travel"]},{"k":"li","s":["follow the advice of local authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["The European Union’s (EU) new Entry/Exit System (EES) is now being implemented across the Schengen area. The EES may take each passenger extra time, so it is important to be prepared to wait longer than usual at EU country borders and allow more time for immigration controls if travelling to and from the Schengen area."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/montenegro/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Montenegro set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Montenegrin Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.me/en/diplomatic-missions/embassies-and-consulates-of-montenegro/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-northern-ireland"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities may close land border crossings at short notice."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Montenegro, your passport must:"]},{"k":"li","s":["have been issued less than 10 years before the date you enter Montenegro – if you renewed your passport before 1 October 2018, it may have a date of issue that is more than 10 years ago"]},{"k":"li","s":["have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the day you plan to leave"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Montenegro without a visa for up to 90 days in any 180-day period. This applies if you travel:"]},{"k":"li","s":["as a tourist"]},{"k":"li","s":["to visit family or friends"]},{"k":"li","s":["to attend business meetings, cultural or sports events"]},{"k":"li","s":["for short-term studies or training"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are travelling to Montenegro without a visa, make sure your whole visit is within the 90-day limit. Visits to Montenegro within the previous 180 days before you travel count towards your 90 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["Montenegro is not part of the ",["Schengen area","https://home-affairs.ec.europa.eu/policies/schengen-borders-and-visa/schengen-area_en"],", so:"]},{"k":"li","s":["visits to Montenegro do not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit in the Schengen area"]},{"k":"li","s":["visits to other EU or Schengen countries do not count towards your 90-day visa-free limit in Montenegro"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped on entry and exit."]},{"k":"p","s":["The dated entry stamp helps avoid any problems about the length of your stay in the country."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Staying longer than 90 days in a 180-day period"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer than 90 days, you must meet the Montenegrin government’s entry requirements. Check which type of visa or work permit you may need with the ",["Montenegrin Embassy in the UK","https://www.gov.me/en/diplomatic-missions/embassies-and-consulates-of-montenegro/united-kingdom-of-great-britain-and-northern-ireland"]," in advance of your arrival to Montenegro."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Montenegro guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/152/montenegro#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["All visitors to Montenegro must register with the local tourism office or police within 24 hours of arrival."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re staying in a hotel or in some holiday lets, the staff or the owner is obliged to register you."]},{"k":"p","s":["If staying in private accommodation, make sure you complete the registration yourself."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not register you may be fined, detained or face a court appearance."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry by sea"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are sailing to Montenegro, enter only at a designated port or harbour. If this is not possible, contact the ",["local harbour master","https://www.luckekapetanije.me/"]," (in Montenegrin) or the police before entering."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into and out of Montenegro."]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare valuable items like expensive jewellery, photographic and computer equipment or anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking pets into Montenegro"]},{"k":"p","s":["Montenegro accepts pet passports. You can bring up to 5 pets, as long as they meet ",["medical and other requirements","https://www.montenegro.travel/en/plan-your-stay-in-montenegro/how-can-you-journey-to-us/conditions-for-entering-montenegro"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking food into Montenegro"]},{"k":"p","s":["You cannot take meat, milk or products containing them into Montenegro. There are some exceptions such as powdered baby milk, baby food and special foods or pet feed required for medical reasons."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Montenegro"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking medicines into Montenegro"]},{"k":"p","s":["When travelling to Montenegro, you may carry a reasonable amount of medication needed for personal use for a maximum of 6 months. You must declare any prescription medication containing narcotics to customs on arrival and may only bring up to 30 days’ worth of such medication, accompanied by a prescription or certificate from a doctor. The certificate must be less than 90 days old."]},{"k":"p","s":["Possession of a medications without proper medical documentation, or failure to declare such medication, may lead to confiscation and legal action."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Montenegro"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there’s no recent history of terrorism in Montenegro, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, keep up to date with local media reports and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political demonstrations"]},{"k":"p","s":["Protests and demonstrations sometimes take place in Montenegro, often in front of government or religious buildings. They are mostly peaceful but can lead to traffic disruption, clashes with police and the potential for violent incidents."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take sensible precautions to protect yourself and your belongings from street crime. Do not leave bags unattended and be wary of pickpockets in tourist hot spots, beaches, airports and on public transport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Use a hotel safe for your valuables and money if possible. Do not leave your luggage in a parked vehicle."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can reduce the risk of bag-snatching and mugging by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoiding isolated areas at night, especially if walking alone"]},{"k":"li","s":["using licensed taxis ordered in advance or using a taxi app"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Lost or stolen passports"]},{"k":"p","s":["If your passport is lost or stolen, you must renew your passport or apply for an emergency travel document. You cannot use a police report to leave Montenegro."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Violent crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Incidents of violent crime between organised criminal groups can affect others close by. Be cautious, remain vigilant and aware of your surroundings. Stay away from confrontations and leave the area if you feel unsafe. In the event of any incidents, follow all advice given by the local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bank card fraud"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fraudsters can steal your card details without you noticing. Use ATMs inside banks if possible, and check ATMs on the street for signs of tampering. Keep cards in sight when paying in shops and restaurants. Read more about ",["how to avoid bank card fraud","https://www.actionfraud.police.uk/a-z-of-fraud/bank-card-and-cheque-fraud"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always carry a form of ID such as a photocard driving licence or passport. If you do not have it with you, the police can give you a fine. Keep a copy of your passport’s photo page in a safe place."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Montenegro have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["Taking photographs of police or military installations, personnel or vehicles is illegal and could lead to arrest and prosecution by the authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["While there is a general tolerance of same-sex couples in Montenegro, LGBT+ travellers should be aware that showing affection in public could receive negative attention. Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Outdoor activities and adventure tourism"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Swimming safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Take note of warning signs on beaches, follow instructions from lifeguards and observe the flag indicators. Take local advice if jellyfish or sea urchins are present. Speedboats and other watercraft operate frequently along the coast, particularly during the summer months. Take care when swimming, remain aware of vessels operating nearby, and use designated swimming areas where available."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["water safety on holiday","https://www.rlss.org.uk/safety-on-holiday"]," from the Royal Life Saving Society."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Paragliding, jet-skis and quad bikes"]},{"k":"p","s":["For all extreme sports and water sports, take precautions to prevent injuries and use protective equipment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Before signing up with paragliding instructors, ask to see their training licence for tandem flights."]},{"k":"p","s":["When renting a jet-ski, you should always get a safety briefing and clear instructions about where you can and cannot ride. See ",["watersports safety abroad","https://www.rospa.com/leisure-water-safety/water/advice/watersports-abroad"]," from the Royal Society for the Prevention of Accidents."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have the appropriate licence and insurance when renting outdoor activity vehicles, such as jet-skis and quad bikes. Take precautions to prevent injuries and use protective equipment. Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Hiking and mountaineering"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hikers have got lost in the mountains when they have left marked paths. If you get into trouble, call the emergency number 112."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re hiking in the mountains:"]},{"k":"li","s":["get expert advice from local guides"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not underestimate the hike, or factors like weather, landscape, distance and elevation"]},{"k":"li","s":["take a fully charged mobile phone and enough supplies"]},{"k":"li","s":["inform someone of your route and expected return time"]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["Traffic congestion is common during the summer tourist season, particularly on coastal roads, major routes and at border crossings. Journey times can be significantly longer than usual. If you are planning to drive in Montenegro, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Montenegro guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/montenegro/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["The standard of roads is fair. Conditions are worse in rural areas, especially in the winter and after bad weather. The 2-lane Moraca Canyon can be dangerous when conditions are poor and there is congestion."]},{"k":"p","s":["Roads leading to Montenegro’s coastal areas are in better condition, but high traffic volumes can lead to delays during the summer season."]},{"k":"p","s":["Occasionally peaceful protests may occur, blocking main roads for several hours."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact the Auto-Moto Association of Montenegro for roadside assistance and information about road closures. Assistance is available in English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: +38219807"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only use officially licensed taxis, which have a taxi sign on the roof and a company name and number written on the side."]},{"k":"p","s":["When using local taxis, always check the price per kilometre or agree on the full fare in advance, to avoid surprises. While many taxi drivers are honest, some may take advantage of tourists by overcharging, as in many other tourist destinations."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are arriving at Podgorica airport, be aware that not all taxi companies are authorised to pick up passengers directly from the airport. To avoid issues, either take one of the licenced taxis available in front of the terminal or, if you are booking a ride in advance, confirm that the driver is permitted to collect passengers at the airport. Whilst there is no fine for passengers of unauthorised taxi pickups, it can cause delays if the driver is pulled aside by the authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Traffic penalties"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you break the speed limit by 10kph, police can fine you. Excessive speeding and overtaking under dangerous conditions are both punishable by automatic confiscation of your driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["The drink-driving limit is less than half the limit in England and Wales."]},{"k":"p","s":["Penalties for traffic offences range from fines of 20 to 6,000 euros to prison sentences."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you get a fine, you may have to pay at a bank or post office within 8 days or before leaving the country. Unpaid fines for foreign nationals are recorded."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are involved in a small traffic accident, you can request a police investigation at a cost of 50 euros. If the other driver is found guilty, they must reimburse you. If you want to appeal the penalty, you have the right to appear in court."]},{"k":"p","s":["If the drivers agree, they can both complete a European accident report and submit it to their insurance companies without a police investigation."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re sailing and want to enter Montenegro, see ",["Entry requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/montenegro/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have had an accident at sea, call 129, the emergency number of the rescue unit within the ",["Maritime Safety Department","https://www.gov.me/clanak/odsjek-traganja-i-spasavanja-na-moru"]," (in Montenegrin)."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Pedestrian safety"]},{"k":"p","s":["Traffic can be busy, fast and chaotic. Take care when crossing roads. Pedestrians should use designated road crossings. You can be fined for crossing the road if you are within 100 metres of a pedestrian crossing but do not use it. Drivers do not always stop, even though they are required to. The green pedestrian crossing signal also allows cars to turn right on to the crossing, so cross with caution."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildfires"]},{"k":"p","s":["Wildfires are common in Montenegro from April to October due to the dry and hot weather. Wildfires are highly dangerous and unpredictable. You should:"]},{"k":"li","s":["take care when visiting or driving through the countryside"]},{"k":"li","s":["make sure cigarette ends are properly extinguished"]},{"k":"li","s":["not light fires or barbecues except in designated and marked areas"]},{"k":"li","s":["not leave any rubbish"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you see a wildfire, call the emergency services on 112. Follow any advice from the police or local authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Flooding"]},{"k":"p","s":["Flooding can be a problem when there is heavy rain and snow melts, causing rivers to flood in winter and spring."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor media reports and follow the advice of the local authorities if flooding occurs in your area."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Montenegro lies in a seismically active zone and small tremors are recorded throughout the year. Serious earthquakes are less frequent but do happen. The last serious earthquake was in 1979. The US Federal Emergency Management Agency’s website tells you about what to do before, during and after an earthquake."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Dial 112 for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance or medical assistance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Montenegro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/152/montenegro#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See what ",["health risks you’ll face in Montenegro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/152/montenegro"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["biting insects and ticks"]},{"k":"li","s":["tick-borne encephalitis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Montenegro. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details of customs rules relating to bringing medication into Montenegro, please see the ",["Entry Requirements","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/montenegro/entry-requirements"]," page."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-and-travel"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Montenegro"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical providers in Montenegro","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/list-of-medical-facilities-in-montenegro"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Health insurance cards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Montenegro recognises the Global Health Insurance Card (GHIC)."]},{"k":"p","s":["The NHS’s ",["getting healthcare abroad webpage","https://www.nhs.uk/using-the-nhs/healthcare-abroad/apply-for-a-free-uk-global-health-insurance-card-ghic/"]," has details about:"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to apply for a GHIC"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to get temporary cover if you lose your card or it does not arrive in time"]},{"k":"li","s":["what special conditions apply in Montenegro"]},{"k":"p","s":["A GHIC is not an alternative to travel insurance. You may have costs your GHIC does not cover."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is also ",["guidance on healthcare if you’re living in Montenegro","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-montenegro#health"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Accessing emergency medical treatment"]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK has a reciprocal healthcare agreement with Montenegro, enabling British nationals to receive free emergency treatment in Montenegro. You must have a valid British passport and the GHIC to apply for a certificate of entitlement from the ",["Montenegrin Health Insurance Fund","https://fzocg.me/podrucne-jedinice/"],", to access free or subsidised medical care at state run medical facilities. You must apply for a certificate in advance or as soon as possible after an urgent admission to hospital. Further details on applying for a Montenegrin Health Insurance Fund can be found in the ",["Living in Montenegro","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/living-in-montenegro#healthcare-in-montenegro"]," guide."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not have a certificate, you will have to pay for the treatment and paid bills cannot be reimbursed."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro.","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travel-and-mental-health"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Montenegro"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you’re involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Montenegro"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Montenegro"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Montenegro"]," in Montenegro"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Montenegro","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/bereavement-guide-for-montenegro/montenegro-bereavement-information"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested in Montenegro","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/montenegro-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/montenegro/british-embassy-podgorica"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/montenegro/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]}],"chars":19809,"change":"New information on wait times if travelling to and from the Schengen area from Montenegro and updated information about road travel and swimming safety ('Warnings and insurance' and ‘Safety and security’ pages)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/moldova":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"262c1dcfc4857047a07e01b27b9f0f09f3698c61b98999f1c934fe0cc14bfb97","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/moldova","bytes":61859,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Moldova travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-01-04T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-11-04T14:54:38+00:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Transnistria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Transnistria. There is widespread military activity in Ukraine, including close to some Moldovan borders. Transnistria is outside the control of the Moldovan government."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO’s ability to offer support is extremely limited and will be more limited if there is military action on or near the Moldova-Ukraine border."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/moldova/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of the current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Moldova set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Moldovan Embassy in the UK","https://regatulunit.mfa.gov.md/en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 3 months after the date you plan to leave Moldova, and at least one blank page."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Moldova for tourism or business without a visa for up to 90 days in a 6-month period. You must be able to show proof of return or onward travel to another country, such as an onward flight ticket."]},{"k":"p","s":["You need a work permit or residence permit to work or for stays of more than 90 days. See ",["more information on work and residence permits","https://mfa.gov.md/en/content/residence-and-work-permits"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Moldovan authorities will automatically register your arrival date. They strictly enforce penalties, including fines and expulsion, against foreign visitors who stay in Moldova longer than allowed. Contact the Moldovan authorities with any additional questions."]},{"k":"h","s":["Land border crossings"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entering and leaving Transnistria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Transnistria."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no internationally recognised boundary between Transnistria and the rest of Moldova. However, Transnistria’s de facto authorities operate checkpoints controlling access to the region, including near the Tighina (Bender) fortress. These checkpoints can be manned by both Transnistrian and Russian guards. Passports will be controlled but will not be stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["When you enter Transnistria, you need to fill in 2 copies of a migration card for the de facto authorities – keep one copy to show them when you leave. The de facto authorities may ask the purpose and length of your visit, and where you will stay. They may also deny you entry."]},{"k":"p","s":["All border crossings between Ukraine and Transnistria are temporarily closed. FCDO does not know when they will reopen."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entering Moldova from Romania"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check for updates on border crossings from Romania with the Moldovan Border Police."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entering Moldova from Ukraine"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been incidents associated with Russia’s war against Ukraine near Moldova–Ukraine border crossings, including temporary suspensions of border operations following nearby drone and missile strikes and falling debris."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check for updates on border crossings from Ukraine with the Moldovan Border Police."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you enter Moldova overland from Ukraine, go to an internationally recognised border crossing point. These are in the north and south of Moldova, excluding the Transnistria region."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have travelled to Moldova from Ukraine and need assistance, call (+373) 22 225 902 or ",["contact FCDO online","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/moldova/british-embassy-chisinau"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re near a Ukraine-Moldova border crossing point and need assistance, call +44 1908 516666 and select option 2: consular services for British nationals."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Entering Ukraine from Moldova"]},{"k":"p","s":["Check for updates on border crossings with Ukraine with the Moldovan Border Police. This is particularly important around Transnistria, which is outside the control of the Moldovan authorities. Read FCDO’s ",["Ukraine travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/ukraine"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Moldova guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/149/moldova#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about ",["goods you can take into or out of Moldova","https://customs.gov.md/en/articles/titlul-en--------------------------------"],". You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Moldova"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 euros or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it in with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Moldova"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there is no recent history of terrorism in Moldova, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["Since Russia’s full scale invasion of Ukraine, drone incursions into Moldovan airspace have occurred. Debris from drones and missiles linked to Russia’s war against Ukraine have also fallen in Moldova."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you encounter debris, do not approach it and follow the directions of local authorities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Occasionally there are protests that can cause disruption. Protests are normally peaceful and well-policed. You should avoid any political demonstrations."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Humanitarian support workers"]},{"k":"p","s":["The UK supports humanitarian efforts in Ukraine and Moldova. If you’re considering providing humanitarian support to Ukrainians in Moldova, check:"]},{"k":"li","s":["updates on the ",["UK government response to the Russian invasion of Ukraine","https://ukstandswithukraine.campaign.gov.uk/"]]},{"k":"li","s":["the ",["Moldovan government’s information","https://dopomoga.gov.md/"]," (largely in Romanian and Russian)"]},{"k":"li","s":["Moldovan Government’s information on ",["bringing in humanitarian supplies","https://dopomoga.gov.md/humanitarian-aid-import"]," (in Romanian and Russian only)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Be alert to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["street crime and petty theft, particularly in Chisinau"]},{"k":"li","s":["pickpockets and bag snatchers in crowded areas and on public transport"]},{"k":"li","s":["credit card and ATM fraud – keep sight of the card when paying a bill"]},{"k":"p","s":["Keep your valuables and passport in a safe place, such as a hotel safe."]},{"k":"p","s":["Streets, pavements and public paths are not well-maintained or well-lit, including in Chisinau and other cities. Consider carrying a torch."]},{"k":"p","s":["Women may experience sexual harassment in Moldova, including on public transport and in parks. Take particular care in the evening and in poorly lit areas. In an emergency, call 112."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Discrimination"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some Asian and Afro-Caribbean visitors have reported being verbally abused or assaulted. Visitors also report police harassment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Police checks and personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent police checks and police officers have the right to ask for ID on the street. Always carry a copy of the photo page of your passport with you."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Buying and exporting art and antiques"]},{"k":"p","s":["You must get permission from the Moldovan Department of Monuments to take any artwork or antiques out of the country. If you do not, customs officials could seize the goods and you could face criminal charges."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras"]},{"k":"p","s":["Avoid taking photos of military and government facilities, including airports and power stations. If caught, authorities are likely to question you and ask you to delete the photos in their presence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Same-sex sexual activity is not illegal in Moldova, but the Moldovan government does not formally recognise same-sex partners. There is an active social and lobbying group on gay and lesbian issues in Chisinau. Public attitudes are less tolerant and showing affection in public can receive unwanted attention."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Surrogacy"]},{"k":"p","s":["Child surrogacy is strictly prohibited throughout Moldova. The British Embassy will not be able to provide support if you get involved in any way."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Illegal drugs, even small quantities of drugs (class A, B or C) including cannabis, carry severe penalties. You should expect a long jail sentence and heavy fines for possessing, using or smuggling illegal drugs, including when transiting through the airport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Airports in Moldova have excellent technology and security for detecting illegal items. This is also used to scan the baggage of transiting passengers."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Paying by card is now generally widespread, however you may not always be able to pay this way, particularly outside the capital, Chisinau."]},{"k":"p","s":["Carry some local currency, euros or US dollars in cash."]},{"k":"p","s":["Notes should be in perfect condition, or they may be refused. You can exchange pound sterling and other major currencies for Moldovan lei at banks and currency exchange offices."]},{"k":"p","s":["ATMs in Transnistrian banks will not accept cards issued outside the region, and foreign cards cannot be used for payments. The currency used in Transnistria is the Transnistrian ruble. Moldovan lei, euros, or US dollars can be exchanged for Transnistrian ruble when in the region. Attempting to pay in currencies other than the Transnistrian ruble is considered illegal by the self-declared authorities. Transnistrian rubles cannot be bought or exchanged outside of Transnistria."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to drive a hire car or a UK vehicle, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the ",["rules of the road in the RAC’s Moldova guide","https://www.rac.co.uk/drive/travel/country/moldova/"],". The guide lists driving regulations and other legal requirements you need to be aware of."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Moldova. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must declare your vehicle to customs if you enter Moldova by car. You can take vehicles into Moldova without paying import taxes for up to 90 days in a 365-day period. The British Embassy cannot help you with bringing vehicles into Moldova. Contact the ",["Moldovan Embassy in the UK","https://regatulunit.mfa.gov.md/en"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check if you need a ",["UK sticker to drive your car outside the UK","https://www.gov.uk/displaying-number-plates/flags-identifiers-and-stickers"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re driving a private vehicle owned by someone else, you need permission from the owner, translated and notarised."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road conditions and driving standards"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving standards are poor and roads are of variable quality. There are many traffic accidents, including fatal ones. Avoid driving outside urban areas when possible, particularly at night."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Drink-driving"]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Moldova. If you are tested and found to have more than a third of England’s legal limit of alcohol in your system, you may get a fine and possible imprisonment."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taxis"]},{"k":"p","s":["Use licensed taxis or reputable ride-hailing services. Official-looking taxis can be unlicensed. Do not share taxis with strangers or flag down unofficial taxis. If there is no meter, negotiate a price before getting into a taxi. Where possible, ask your hotel to order you a taxi or give you the number of a reputable company. Confirm the driver’s identity and license plate before getting into the car."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Earthquakes"]},{"k":"p","s":["Moldova has insignificant earth tremors throughout the year. The last significant earthquake occurred in 1986, causing deaths and damage to buildings."]},{"k":"p","s":["The US Federal Emergency Management Agency website has advice about ",["what to do before, during and after an earthquake","https://www.ready.gov/earthquakes"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Moldova. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/moldova"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/moldova/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transnistria"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Transnistria."]},{"k":"p","s":["Transnistria is outside the control of the Moldovan government. There is widespread military activity in Ukraine, including close to some Moldovan borders."]},{"k":"p","s":["All border crossings between Ukraine and Transnistria are temporarily closed."]},{"k":"p","s":["The self-declared Transnistrian parliament has increased powers for prosecutions and pre-trial detentions against people regarded as extremists. They interpret extremism as including many activities that British nationals would consider legitimate, including moderate protest or freedom of expression."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 112 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Staff may only speak Russian or Romanian."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Moldova","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/149/moldova#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Moldova","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/149/moldova"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["biting insects and ticks"]},{"k":"li","s":["tick-borne encephalitis"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Water quality"]},{"k":"p","s":["Only drink bottled or boiled water."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Moldova"]},{"k":"p","s":["State medical facilities in Moldova are generally poor. Private clinics and hospitals offer a better standard of care. If you are involved in an accident or taken ill, it is likely that you would be taken to a state hospital."]},{"k":"p","s":["Most medical service providers in Moldova will expect cash or card payment for their services at the time of treatment. Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment and repatriation."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a list of ",["medical facilities in Moldova","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/moldova-list-of-medical-facilities-and-practitioners"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Moldova"]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Moldova"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Moldova"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Moldova"]," in Moldova"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Moldova","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/moldova-bereavement-packinformation"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Moldova","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/moldova-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/moldova/british-embassy-chisinau"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/moldova/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Moldova","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-moldova"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":16971,"change":"This travel advice has been reviewed for accuracy with changes made throughout, including updated information about visa requirements, land border crossings, entering Moldova from Ukraine, political situation, humanitarian support workers, crime, using cameras, money and taxi's ('Entry requirements'"},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mongolia":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"c8435051871910484c151365fbca5b9335d7b9d6f7ca5b71ec1d25f612874f5c","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/mongolia","bytes":71048,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Mongolia travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-04T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-07T13:03:24+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"h","s":["Fuel shortages in Mongolia"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are reports of fuel shortages in Mongolia, including aviation fuel. Fuel supply disruptions may affect domestic and international flights, road travel and access to some remote areas. Check with your airline or transport provider before travelling, allow extra time for journeys and follow advice from the local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Before you travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["No travel can be guaranteed safe. Read all the advice in this guide. You may also find it helpful to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for women travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/advice-for-women-travelling-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read our ",["guide on disability and travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/disabled-travellers"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["general advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"]]},{"k":"li","s":["read about ",["safety for solo and independent travel","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/solo-and-independent-travel"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see ",["advice on volunteering and adventure travel abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/safer-adventure-travel-and-volunteering-overseas"]]},{"k":"hs","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mongolia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["Travel Aware on Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/accounts/login/?next=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.instagram.com%2Ftravelaware%2F&is_from_rle"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Mongolia’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Mongolia set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Mongolian Embassy in the UK","https://embassyofmongolia.co.uk/?lang=en"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Mongolia, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can visit Mongolia for tourism purposes for up to 30 days without a visa until 31 December 2026."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Applying for a visa"]},{"k":"p","s":["To stay longer, to work or study, for business travel or for other reasons you must ",["meet the Mongolian government’s entry requirements","https://immigration.gov.mn/en/vizijn-zvshrl/"],". For more details, contact the ",["Mongolian Embassy in the UK","https://embassyofmongolia.co.uk/?lang=en"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure the border control officer puts a stamp in your passport or you could face issues when leaving the country."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travelling with children"]},{"k":"p","s":["Adults accompanying children other than their own should have a notarised letter from the parents or legal guardian to confirm the arrangement."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["For details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Mongolia guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/151/mongolia#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Registering with the authorities"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your hotel or landlord will register you using an app. If you are travelling independently or staying with friends, you must register yourself with the ",["Mongolian Immigration Agency","https://immigration.gov.mn/en/"],". You do not need to go in person."]},{"k":"p","s":["The agency will issue you with a digital residence permit that shows your passport number, address, photograph and fingerprints. Always carry it when you are in Mongolia."]},{"k":"h","s":["Borders with Mongolia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mongolia takes border security very seriously and foreign nationals are not routinely allowed access to border areas. The authorities can regard zones of up to 100km inside the border as a border area. If you wish to travel in these areas, you must get permission from the State Frontier Guard Authority. Only a few specified land border crossings are open to foreigners."]},{"k":"h","s":["Borders within Mongolia"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is currently a Foot and Mouth Disease outbreak in the western provinces of Khovd, Bayan-Ulgii, Govi-Altai and Selenge in Mongolia. Mongolian authorities are taking action to stop the outbreak spreading further but other Mongolian provinces could be affected at short notice. Monitor local media for the latest information."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Border points open to British citizens"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are normally 8 border points open to British passport holders:"]},{"k":"li","s":["Chinggis Khaan International Airport in Ulaanbaatar"]},{"k":"li","s":["Zamin Uud – road and train crossing to China"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bulgan – road crossing to China in the west"]},{"k":"li","s":["Bichigt – road crossing to China in the south-east"]},{"k":"li","s":["Tsagaannuur – road crossing to Russia in the far west"]},{"k":"li","s":["Sukhbaatar – train crossing to Russia"]},{"k":"li","s":["Altanbulag – road crossing to Russia"]},{"k":"li","s":["Ereen-Tsav – road crossing to Russia"]},{"k":"p","s":["You may not cross into China or Russia at other border points, as they are only open to Mongolians, Chinese or Russians."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you travel by train across the China-Mongolia border, expect a delay of a few hours as the railways use different gauges."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is difficult to get visas for China or Russia in Mongolia. Ask the Chinese and Russian embassies in London about their visa requirements before travelling to Mongolia."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Mongolia-Russia border"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can only enter Mongolia from Russia on public buses, trains, taxis or private vehicles. All international flights are suspended."]},{"k":"p","s":["Russian border officials will carefully examine your travel documents."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you have arrived in Mongolia from Russia and need assistance, call +976 (11) 458 133 and select the option ‘consular services for British nationals’."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Mongolia. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you become involved in a commercial dispute or a criminal investigation about a customs matter, you may be held in Mongolia until it is resolved. Ask to speak to the British Embassy, especially if the authorities say you must accept a travel ban."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Bringing your vehicle to Mongolia"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you plan to enter Mongolia at a land border crossing in your own vehicle, inform the tax authorities and border troops in advance. Contact ",["Mongolian Customs","https://www.customs.gov.mn/en/"]," (in Mongolian). You must complete a customs declaration form. You can do this at the border or at Ulaanbaatar City Customs Office, next to the train station. Make sure you have your driving licence and all the vehicle documents, including ownership records and insurance."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you do not leave Mongolia in the vehicle you used to enter the country, you must pay customs tax. The amount of tax depends on the vehicle’s engine size and value. For information, see ",["Mongolian Customs","https://www.customs.gov.mn/en/"]," (in Mongolian)."]},{"k":"p","s":["If your vehicle breaks down and cannot be fixed, you must pay for it to be transported out of Mongolia or sell it to a local mechanic."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you sell your broken-down vehicle to a mechanic, you must still pay customs tax when you leave. You must show the customs office evidence you sold the vehicle (proof of sale document, photos, a letter from the mechanic and a police report)."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must not leave your vehicle unattended or abandon it. If you do, Mongolian Customs will contact the British Embassy and send you a fine. If you leave your vehicle in Mongolia, you must pay to store it with a mechanic or at an official customs warehouse. When you leave the country, you must submit a customs declaration form and show your driving licence, car ownership records and proof of valid insurance."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Mongolia"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can take in up to 15 million in Mongolian tugriks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare cash or travellers cheques if the value is 10,000 US dollars or more. You will get a certified declaration to show you brought it with you. If you do not, your money could be seized when you leave."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Mongolia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although there is no recent history of terrorism in Mongolia, attacks cannot be ruled out."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been occasional instances of civil and political unrest resulting in protests. Avoid large gatherings and demonstrations for your personal safety."]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Pickpockets may operate in markets and crowded public places. The risk increases during the festivals of Tsagaan Sar (New Year, celebrated from December to February) and Naadam (July). Take extra precautions during these periods."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["Occasionally large groups of people, including children and teenagers, harass pedestrians for money as they get into vehicles or walk into pubs or restaurants. Keep your mobile phone, passport and money in a secured bag on your person, and leave valuables in a hotel safe if possible."]},{"k":"p","s":["Violent incidents are rare, but foreigners have been assaulted and robbed in Ulaanbaatar. Avoid being out alone at night, and ask hotels, restaurants or clubs to order a car for you. If hailing a ride, use only licensed taxis such as VIP Taxis. Alternatively use the taxi app UBCab, which is trackable."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Reporting crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Mongolian government has asked foreigners to report crimes so they can investigate and keep records. You do not need to have any further involvement and will be free to leave once you’ve made your report."]},{"k":"p","s":["In an emergency call the police on 102 or +976 102 from an international mobile phone. There should be someone available on this number who can speak to you in English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["Always carry your passport. If the police ask you for ID they will not accept a copy and you could be fined. Keep copies of the photo page and the page with your Mongolian entry stamp in a separate place."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are a resident, carry your registration card."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Respecting religious customs"]},{"k":"p","s":["Show respect in Buddhist monasteries. Always ask for permission to take photographs and do not touch sacred images or objects."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to possess or use any type of drugs, including cannabis. If you are found guilty of drug trafficking, you could face a life sentence. Mongolian prisons have very basic facilities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to photograph or video police, police escorts or military personnel. You could be arrested and fined. The court decides the fine based on the degree of social danger of the crime and the income of the defendant."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["Although not illegal, same-sex relationships are not generally accepted socially."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Wildlife, animal products and souvenirs"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to buy, sell, kill or capture any protected species of wild animal or trade its parts without a licence. You could get a fine and a prison sentence."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Phone and wifi coverage"]},{"k":"p","s":["Most UK phone networks operate in the cities and wifi is widely available in hotels, restaurants and bars, especially in Ulaanbaatar. You can buy local SIM cards and mobile phones. In rural Mongolia there are large areas that do not have network coverage."]},{"k":"h","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Mongolia, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"],". You need a ",["1968 international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," and a UK driving licence. The 1949 IDP is not accepted any more. You cannot buy an IDP outside the UK, so get one before you travel."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards and road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are a high number of road accidents, due to:"]},{"k":"li","s":["low driving standards"]},{"k":"li","s":["speeding"]},{"k":"li","s":["poorly maintained vehicles"]},{"k":"li","s":["difficult terrain"]},{"k":"li","s":["dangerous road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Driving in Ulaanbaatar is hazardous as roads are heavily congested. Outside the capital, only about 10% of the country’s roads are tarmacked and signposting is minimal. If you are planning to drive in rural Mongolia, prepare by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["researching your route"]},{"k":"li","s":["asking local guides or drivers about the road conditions ahead"]},{"k":"li","s":["checking ",["World Meteorological Organization weather forecasts for Mongolia","https://worldweather.wmo.int/en/country.html?countryCode=MNG"]]},{"k":"li","s":["taking back-up communication devices such as a satellite phone"]},{"k":"li","s":["packing plenty of water and provisions"]},{"k":"li","s":["sharing details of your route and expected arrival and departure times"]},{"k":"p","s":["Mongolia does not have an extensive road network and driving can be dangerous due to the terrain."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to ",["prepare for and respond to extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mongolia is a huge country with varying weather conditions from +35°C in summer to -40°C in winter and during the nights. Weather conditions often change without warning."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are frequent weather warnings all year round for flooding, dust storms, heavy snow and blizzards, strong winds and heatwaves."]},{"k":"p","s":["The most extreme weather conditions occur in and around the Gobi Desert and the Steppes. Check the ",["World Meteorological Organization weather forecasts for Mongolia","https://worldweather.wmo.int/en/country.html?countryCode=MNG"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 103 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine recommendations and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Mongolia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/151/mongolia#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Mongolia","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/151/mongolia"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Altitude sickness is a risk in parts of Mongolia. Read more about ",["altitude sickness on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/26/altitude-illness"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The high levels of air pollution in Ulaanbaatar, especially in winter, may aggravate bronchial, sinus or asthma conditions. Children, the elderly and those with pre-existing medical conditions may be especially affected. You can check the levels for Ulaanbaatar on the ",["Real-time Air Quality Index","https://www.aqicn.info/city/ulaanbaatar"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["It is best to bring prescription medication and a first aid kit with you. Medical products in pharmacies are mainly from China and Russia, so you may not easily recognise what you need."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Mongolia"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no reciprocal healthcare agreements between the UK and Mongolia, so you cannot get free healthcare in Mongolia."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are injured or become ill in a remote part of the country, it may be a long journey to the nearest medical facility. Outside Ulaanbaatar, the standard of healthcare is limited, and doctors may not speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["At hospitals, you will have to pay 80% of the treatment cost in advance. Make sure you have access to funds and that your insurance covers:"]},{"k":"li","s":["full medical expenses"]},{"k":"li","s":["an air ambulance, in case you need to be flown home"]},{"k":"li","s":["bringing a body home in the event of a death"]},{"k":"li","s":["bringing your family home, if one of you is seriously ill or injured"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Mongolia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mongolia-list-of-medical-facilities"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Mongolia"]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 103"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 101"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 102 (includes traffic police)"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Mongolia"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Mongolia"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Mongolia"]," in Mongolia"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Mongolia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mongolia-bereavement-information-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Mongolia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mongolia-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad"]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["how to get help from the UK government abroad","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/mongolia/british-embassy-ulaanbaatar"]," including in an emergency."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help in the UK"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Get travel advice updates"]},{"k":"p","s":["Sign up to ",["get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mongolia/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO:"]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on X","https://x.com/fcdotravelgovuk"]]},{"k":"li","s":[["travel advice on Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/FCDOTravel/"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Mongolia","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-mongolia"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":17120,"change":"New information on fuel shortages in Mongolia (‘Warnings and insurance’ page)."},"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mozambique":{"r":"govuk","at":"2026-11-17T17:03Z","sha":"7bb34393c0ccea67219455470b979483ab31752fb6e9d7e545f446c37861e981","read":"https://www.gov.uk/api/content/foreign-travel-advice/mozambique","bytes":82226,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Mozambique travel advice","by":[{"n":"Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","r":""}],"pub":"2013-03-18T00:00:00+00:00","mod":"2026-08-20T14:50:43+01:00","blocks":[{"k":"h","s":["Warnings and insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["Your travel insurance could be invalidated if you travel against advice from the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO)."]},{"k":"h","s":["Areas where FCDO advises against travel"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Cabo Delgado Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Cabo Delgado Province, except for Palma town and the area around Pemba and Afungi."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all but essential travel to Palma town and the area around Pemba and Afungi."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Nampula Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the districts of Memba and Eráti in Nampula Province."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Niassa Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the districts of Mecula and Marrupa in Niassa Province."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["why FCDO advises against travel","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mozambique/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel insurance"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you choose to travel, research your destinations and ",["get appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"],". Insurance should cover your itinerary, planned activities and expenses in an emergency."]},{"k":"h","s":["About FCDO travel advice"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO provides advice about risks of travel to help you make informed decisions. Find out ",["more about FCDO travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow FCDO travel on ",["Twitter","https://twitter.com/fcdotravelgovuk"],", ",["Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/fcdotravel"]," and ",["Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"],". You can also ",["sign up to get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mozambique/email-signup"]," when this advice is updated."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entry requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["This information is for people travelling on a full ",["‘British citizen’ passport","https://www.gov.uk/types-of-british-nationality"]," from the UK. It is based on the UK government’s understanding of Mozambique’s current rules for the most common types of travel."]},{"k":"p","s":["The authorities in Mozambique set and enforce entry rules. If you’re not sure how these requirements apply to you, contact the ",["Mozambican High Commission in the UK","https://www.mozambiquehighcommission.org.uk/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Passport validity requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Mozambique, your passport must have an ‘expiry date’ at least 6 months after the date you arrive."]},{"k":"p","s":["Check with your travel provider that your passport and other travel documents meet requirements. ",["Renew your passport","https://www.gov.uk/renew-adult-passport/renew"]," if you need to."]},{"k":"p","s":["You will be denied entry if you do not have a valid travel document or try to use a passport that has been reported lost or stolen."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you get your passport stamped with the correct dates before leaving the immigration desk."]},{"k":"p","s":["You need at least 2 blank pages for entry stamps."]},{"k":"h","s":["Dual nationals"]},{"k":"p","s":["When returning to the UK, British citizens must carry a valid ",["British passport","https://www.gov.uk/browse/abroad/passports"]," or ",["certificate of entitlement","https://www.gov.uk/right-of-abode/apply-for-a-certificate-of-entitlement"],". See ",["Dual citizenship","https://www.gov.uk/dual-citizenship"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travellers under 18"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re entering Mozambique with a child under the age of 18, you will need to present an unabridged birth certificate listing both parents. Where the child is travelling with one parent, or without either parent, a notarised parental consent affidavit (not older than three months) is required."]},{"k":"h","s":["Visa requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["British passport holders must get an Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA) before travelling to Mozambique for tourism or business visits of up to 30 days."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can apply for an ETA through the ",["official Mozambique eVisa portal","https://evisa.gov.mz/"]," at least 5 working days before you travel. You must pay online when you apply. You cannot pay on arrival at the border."]},{"k":"p","s":["The fee is approximately 47 US dollars, including a 37 US dollars visa fee and a 650 Mozambican Metical processing fee. Processing can take at least 5 working days. You should apply well in advance of your travel date."]},{"k":"p","s":["When you arrive in Mozambique, you may be asked to show:"]},{"k":"li","s":["proof of accommodation"]},{"k":"li","s":["a return or onward ticket"]},{"k":"li","s":["proof that you have enough money to support yourself during your stay"]},{"k":"p","s":["You should carry a printed copy of your approved ETA and payment confirmation, as immigration officials may ask to see them when you enter or leave Mozambique."]},{"k":"h","s":["Entering Mozambique by land crossing"]},{"k":"p","s":["Not all lands borders are open 24 hours a day 7 days a week. Check the opening times directly ",["online","https://evisa.gov.mz/"],". Land border crossings into neighbouring countries can be restricted, blocked or closed at short notice."]},{"k":"p","s":["It can take a long time to clear border formalities at the Lebombo-Ressano Garcia land crossing from South Africa, especially during holiday periods. There can be delays if you are travelling on public transport. Allow time to get to your destination before nightfall."]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been armed robberies close to the Lebombo border in Nelspruit. These often take place in the queue for the border, mainly after dark. When you stop at junctions or in queues, stay alert and ensure you have space to turn and drive off."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel to or from South Africa"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re planning to enter South Africa before or after you visit Mozambique, or if you’re planning to travel through South Africa, check the ",["travel advice for South Africa","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/south-africa/entry-requirements"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Vaccine requirements"]},{"k":"p","s":["To enter Mozambique, you must have a certificates to prove you’ve had:"]},{"k":"li","s":["a yellow fever vaccination if you’re coming from a ",["country listed as a transmission risk","https://nathnacyfzone.org.uk/factsheet/65/countries-with-risk-of-yellow-fever-transmission"]]},{"k":"li","s":["a polio vaccine in certain circumstances"]},{"k":"p","s":["For full details about medical entry requirements and recommended vaccinations, see ",["TravelHealthPro’s Mozambique guide","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/155/mozambique#Vaccine_Recommendations"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Customs rules"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are strict rules about goods you can take into or out of Mozambique. You must declare anything that may be prohibited or subject to tax or duty."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Taking money into Mozambique"]},{"k":"p","s":["Declare 10,000 Mozambican meticais or more in cash. Declare foreign cash or travellers cheques if the value is 5,000 US dollars or more."]},{"k":"h","s":["Safety and security"]},{"k":"p","s":["This guide also has safety advice for ",["regions of Mozambique","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mozambique/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorism"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a high threat of terrorist attack globally affecting UK interests and British nationals, including from groups and individuals who view the UK and British nationals as targets. Stay aware of your surroundings at all times."]},{"k":"p","s":["UK Counter Terrorism Policing has information and advice on ",["staying safe","https://www.counterterrorism.police.uk/runhidetell/"]," and what to do in the event of a terrorist attack. Find out ",["how to reduce your risk from terrorism while abroad","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/reduce-your-risk-from-terrorism-while-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Terrorism in Mozambique"]},{"k":"p","s":["Terrorists are very likely to try to carry out attacks in Mozambique."]},{"k":"p","s":["The main threat is from IS-Mozambique (IS-M), a terrorist group with links to Daesh (formerly known as Islamic State) that is mainly active in Cabo Delgado Province, and has carried out attacks in neighbouring districts of Niassa and Nampula Provinces."]},{"k":"p","s":["IS-M militants have conducted violent attacks using explosives, machetes and firearms across Cabo Delgado, resulting in hundreds of deaths, including civilians and security personnel. They have also engaged in burning vehicles and homes, robberies, looting and threats. In 2021, dozens of people were killed in a large scale attack in Palma, Cabo Delgado Province. In these incidents, security forces have not been able to reach these areas quickly."]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["regional risks","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mozambique/regional-risks"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["Attacks could be indiscriminate, including in places frequented by foreign nationals, such as:"]},{"k":"li","s":["roads and road blocks"]},{"k":"li","s":["military bases"]},{"k":"li","s":["towns and villages"]},{"k":"li","s":["islands off the coast"]},{"k":"li","s":["safari or hunting parks"]},{"k":"p","s":["Stay aware of your surroundings, stay up to date with local media reports, and follow the advice of local authorities."]},{"k":"h","s":["Terrorist kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["Due to the presence of groups with links to Islamist extremism, there is a threat of kidnap in Mozambique. The threat is particularly acute in Cabo Delgado Province, as well as neighbouring districts of Niassa and Nampula Provinces."]},{"k":"p","s":["British nationals are seen as legitimate targets, including tourists, humanitarian aid workers, journalists and business travellers. If you are kidnapped, the reason for your presence is unlikely to protect you or secure your safe release."]},{"k":"p","s":["The long-standing policy of the British government policy is not to make substantive concessions to hostage takers. The British government considers that paying ransoms and releasing prisoners builds the capability of terrorist groups and finances their activities. This can, in turn, increase the risk of further hostage-taking. The Terrorism Act (2000) makes payments to terrorists illegal."]},{"k":"p","s":["If you work in Mozambique, you should follow your employer’s security guidelines. Employers are strongly advised to take professional security advice, be vigilant at all times and review security measures regularly. Keep others informed of your travel plans and vary your routines. Make sure your accommodation is secure and consider pre-deployment training or travelling under close protection, particularly if working in Cabo Delgado."]},{"k":"h","s":["Political situation"]},{"k":"p","s":["In Mozambique, protests can occur at short notice and even peaceful protests can become violent. Road toll gates are particularly vulnerable."]},{"k":"p","s":["Access to land borders can be affected at short notice, along with public services and transport."]},{"k":"p","s":["To reduce your personal risk:"]},{"k":"li","s":["seek local advice and monitor the local media"]},{"k":"li","s":["avoid large gatherings or demonstrations"]},{"k":"li","s":["pay attention to your surroundings"]},{"k":"li","s":["do not travel after dark"]},{"k":"h","s":["Crime"]},{"k":"p","s":["Street crime is common in Maputo and is increasing in other cities and tourist destinations. This has involved knives and firearms. There are some areas in cities which are more dangerous – seek local advice. Beaches and offshore islands are not policed."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Protecting yourself and your belongings"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can reduce the risk from pickpocketing and mugging by:"]},{"k":"li","s":["not walking alone, especially in deserted areas or at night"]},{"k":"li","s":["not displaying cash, jewellery or mobile phones"]},{"k":"li","s":["not using ATMs at night, and using ATMs in banks whenever possible"]},{"k":"li","s":["keeping valuables in a hotel safe or other secure place"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you want to report a crime, contact the local police to get a police report. Also report stolen passports to the ",["British High Commission in Maputo","https://www.gov.uk/government/world/organisations/british-high-commission-maputo"]," and the Mozambican immigration authorities."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Carjacking"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a risk of carjacking. Keep your car doors locked and windows closed while driving. Be particularly vigilant when you arrive at or leave residential properties after dark. Avoid driving alone at night."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not pick up strangers or stop to help distressed motorists or pedestrians. Hijackers sometimes use these techniques to trick motorists into stopping their vehicles. If in doubt, drive directly to a police station."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Police harassment and corruption"]},{"k":"p","s":["Some visitors to Mozambique report being victims of police harassment and intimidation, including robbery and requests for bribes. If a police officer threatens you or asks for a bribe, report this to the British High Commission for awareness."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Criminal kidnap"]},{"k":"p","s":["There have been kidnappings for ransom reported in Mozambique, mainly in the capital of Maputo. Kidnaps are generally for financial gain or motivated by criminality. While most victims have been Mozambicans, kidnappers may also target foreigners. Business owners are likely to be at increased risk of this activity. If you work in Mozambique, follow your employer’s security guidelines. Be vigilant at all times."]},{"k":"h","s":["Laws and cultural differences"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Personal ID"]},{"k":"p","s":["As a foreigner, you must always have your passport with you. Police patrols and checkpoints are common, and they will not accept copies or photos."]},{"k":"p","s":["Do not hand over your passport to anyone other than an official. Ask to see their ID if in doubt."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Alcohol laws and bans"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to drink alcohol on public beaches."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Illegal drugs and prison sentences"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are convicted of drug use, possession or trafficking, you can expect to get a long prison sentence and a fine."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Landmines"]},{"k":"p","s":["All known minefields in Mozambique have been cleared. In the central and southern provinces of Sofala, Tete, Manica, Gaza, Inhambane and Maputo, mines may still exist in remote areas away from main routes. Get advice from district authorities if you plan to travel in these areas."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Using cameras in secure areas"]},{"k":"p","s":["It is illegal to photograph government offices, airports, military establishments, residences and police or officials without special permission. If in doubt, do not take pictures."]},{"k":"hs","s":["LGBT+ travellers"]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no laws against same-sex sexual activity. Attitudes in Maputo tend to be more liberal than in more remote rural areas of the country. Read more ",["advice for LGBT+ travellers","https://www.gov.uk/lesbian-gay-bisexual-and-transgender-foreign-travel-advice"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Money"]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you can access money in a variety of ways. Travellers’ cheques are not commonly accepted, Mastercard is not always accepted across the country. US dollars and South African rand are the main exchange currencies."]},{"k":"p","s":["Credit cards, are increasingly accepted in the larger cities. You should tell your bank before using your card in Mozambique."]},{"k":"h","s":["Transport risks"]},{"k":"hs","s":["Road travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you are planning to drive in Mozambique, see ",["information on driving abroad","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad"]," and check the rules of the road."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can use a UK photocard driving licence to drive in Mozambique for up to 90 days. If you still have a paper driving licence, you may need to ",["update it to a photocard licence","https://www.gov.uk/exchange-paper-driving-licence"]," or get the ",["correct version of the international driving permit (IDP)","https://www.gov.uk/driving-abroad/international-driving-permit"]," as well."]},{"k":"p","s":["After 90 days, you must have an IDP or a Mozambican driving licence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Drink-driving is a serious offence in Mozambique. If you are tested and found to have more than three-quarters of England’s legal limit of alcohol in your system, you may get a fine and possible imprisonment."]},{"k":"p","s":["You are legally required have third-party insurance, which you can buy at most land borders. Traffic police may give you an on-the-spot fine if you cannot show your licence and ownership and insurance documents."]},{"k":"p","s":["You must always carry 2 reflective triangles in your vehicle and wear a reflective vest when repairing, loading or unloading a vehicle. If you cannot produce the 2 triangles and 2 vests, you can get an on-the-spot fine."]},{"k":"p","s":["Police officers frequently stop drivers to check paperwork and sometimes try to extract bribes. If police are fining you for no clear reason, ask for a written fine you can pay at a police station."]},{"k":"p","s":["Only travel by road outside major cities during daylight. Where possible, keep to major roads and travel in convoy in rural areas. Fuel supplies at petrol stations throughout Mozambique can be unpredictable and inconsistent, including in major cities. Where fuel is available, queues can be long. Travellers are advised to check with tour operators in advance to ensure sufficient fuel is available for any organised travel, and to allow extra time for journeys."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Driving standards and road conditions"]},{"k":"p","s":["Traffic accidents are common in Mozambique due to poor road conditions and low driving standards. Watch for pedestrians on the roads."]},{"k":"p","s":["Low-lying areas around major rivers flood regularly and at short notice during the rainy season from November to April, making many roads impassable including in the capital, Maputo. Check conditions before travelling. Make sure you have emergency supplies, including a first aid kit."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Public transport"]},{"k":"p","s":["Overland travel on public transport can be hazardous due to vehicles being in an unsafe condition. If you doubt a vehicle’s condition, make alternative arrangements."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Sea travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is a significant risk of ",["piracy in the Gulf of Aden and Indian Ocean","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/sea-river-and-piracy-safety"],". Pirates can attack up to 1,000 nautical miles from the Somali coast or more. The threat assessment of the combined international naval counter-piracy forces is that sailing yachts should not enter the ",["designated high-risk area,","https://on-shore.mschoa.org/"]," due to the risk of hijacking."]},{"k":"h","s":["Extreme weather and natural disasters"]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out what you can do to prepare for and respond to ",["extreme weather and natural hazards","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/tropical-cyclones"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Cyclones and floods"]},{"k":"p","s":["Cyclones and floods are common during the rainy season from November to April. They often cause landslides, which result in road closures and disruption to travel and public transport."]},{"k":"p","s":["Monitor local reports and international weather updates from the ",["World Meteorological Organization","https://severeweather.wmo.int/tc/swi/index.html"]," and the ",["National Meteorological Institute (in Portuguese)","https://www.inam.gov.mz/"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["This section has safety advice for regions of Mozambique. It only covers regions where the Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) has specific advice."]},{"k":"p","s":["You should also read ",["FCDO’s overall travel advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mozambique"]," and ",["safety and security advice","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mozambique/safety-and-security"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Cabo Delgado Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to Cabo Delgado, except Palma town and the area around Pemba and Afungi, due to attacks by groups with links to Islamist extremism and clashes between insurgents, armed vigilante groups and Mozambican security forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["Security forces have set up roadblocks throughout the province."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are no direct flights between Palma town and Maputo and we advise against travelling there by road."]},{"k":"h","s":["Nampula Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advises against all travel to the districts of Memba and Eráti in Nampula Province due to attacks by groups with links to Islamist extremism."]},{"k":"h","s":["Niassa Province"]},{"k":"p","s":["Groups with links to Islamist extremism have previously carried out attacks in the Mecula, Mavago and Marrupa districts of Niassa Province."]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO advise against all travel to the Mecula and Marrupa districts of Niassa Province. There have been recent lethal attacks there within Niassa Special Reserve at hunting lodges visited by international tourists. Groups with links to Islamic extremism have previously carried out attacks in the Mavago district as well, stay aware of your surroundings in this area, as the situation may change without warning."]},{"k":"h","s":["Health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Before you travel check that:"]},{"k":"li","s":["your destination can provide the healthcare you may need"]},{"k":"li","s":["you have ",["appropriate travel insurance","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-insurance"]," for local treatment or unexpected medical evacuation"]},{"k":"p","s":["This is particularly important if you have a health condition or are pregnant."]},{"k":"p","s":["Mozambique is currently experiencing a cholera outbreak in central and northern areas of the country. See ",["information on cholera","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/disease/32/cholera"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency medical number"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 848888 or 823388 and ask for an ambulance."]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your insurance company quickly if you’re referred to a medical facility for treatment."]},{"k":"h","s":["Recommended vaccines and health risks"]},{"k":"p","s":["At least 8 weeks before your trip:"]},{"k":"li","s":["check the latest ",["vaccine recommendations for Mozambique","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/155/mozambique#Vaccine_Recommendations"]]},{"k":"li","s":["see where to get vaccines and whether you have to pay on the ",["NHS travel vaccinations page","https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/travel-vaccinations/"]]},{"k":"p","s":["See ",["what health risks you’ll face in Mozambique","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/country/155/mozambique"]," including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["malaria"]},{"k":"li","s":["dengue"]},{"k":"li","s":["schistosomiasis"]},{"k":"li","s":["mpox"]},{"k":"h","s":["Medication"]},{"k":"p","s":["The legal status and regulation of some medicines prescribed or bought in the UK can be different in other countries."]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["best practice when travelling with medicines on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/43/medicines-abroad"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Healthcare in Mozambique"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has a ",["list of medical providers in Mozambique","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mozambique-list-of-medical-facilties/mozambique-list-of-medical-facilties"]," where some staff will speak English."]},{"k":"p","s":["Hospital facilities are of a lower standard compared to the UK, especially in the north of the country. In cases of serious illness or injury, medical evacuation to South Africa or the UK may be necessary."]},{"k":"p","s":["Make sure you have adequate travel health insurance and accessible funds to cover the cost of any medical treatment abroad and repatriation."]},{"k":"h","s":["Travel and mental health"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read ",["FCDO guidance on travel and mental health","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/foreign-travel-advice-for-people-with-mental-health-issues"],". There is also ",["mental health guidance on TravelHealthPro","https://travelhealthpro.org.uk/factsheet/85/travelling-with-mental-health-conditions"],"."]},{"k":"h","s":["Getting help"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office (FCDO) cannot provide tailored advice for individual trips. Read this travel advice and carry out your own research before deciding whether to travel."]},{"k":"h","s":["Emergency services in Mozambique"]},{"k":"p","s":["Call 112 (ambulance, fire, police)"]},{"k":"p","s":["If the call does not connect, use the country-based numbers or contact your nearest police station or medical facility."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ambulance: 848888 or 823388"]},{"k":"p","s":["Fire: 198"]},{"k":"p","s":["Police: 112"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contact your travel provider and insurer"]},{"k":"p","s":["Contact your travel provider and your insurer if you are involved in a serious incident or emergency abroad. They will tell you if they can help and what you need to do."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Refunds and changes to travel"]},{"k":"p","s":["For refunds or changes to travel, contact your travel provider. You may also be able to make a claim through insurance. However, insurers usually require you to talk to your travel provider first."]},{"k":"p","s":["Find out more about ",["changing or cancelling travel plans","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/about-foreign-commonwealth-development-office-travel-advice#changing-or-cancelling-travel-plans"],", including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["where to get advice if you are in a dispute with a provider"]},{"k":"li","s":["how to access previous versions of travel advice to support a claim"]},{"k":"h","s":["Support from FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["FCDO has guidance on staying safe and what to do if you need help or support abroad, including:"]},{"k":"li","s":["finding English-speaking ",["lawyers","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/lawyers?country=Mozambique"],", ",["funeral directors","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/funeral-directors?country=Mozambique"]," and ",["translators and interpreters","https://find-a-professional-service-abroad.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/find/translators-interpreters?country=Mozambique"]," in Mozambique"]},{"k":"li","s":["dealing with a ",["death in Mozambique","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mozambique-bereavement-packinformation"]]},{"k":"li","s":["being ",["arrested or imprisoned in Mozambique","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mozambique-prisoner-pack"]]},{"k":"li","s":["getting help if you’re a ",["victim of crime","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/victim-of-crime-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["what to do if you’re ",["in hospital","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/in-hospital-abroad"]]},{"k":"li","s":["if you’re ",["affected by a crisis","https://www.gov.uk/guidance/how-to-deal-with-a-crisis-overseas"],", such as a terrorist attack"]},{"k":"h","s":["Contacting FCDO"]},{"k":"p","s":["Follow and contact FCDO travel on ",["Twitter","https://twitter.com/fcdotravelgovuk"],", ",["Facebook","https://www.facebook.com/fcdotravel"]," and ",["Instagram","https://www.instagram.com/travelaware/"],". You can also ",["sign up to get email notifications","https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/mozambique/email-signup"]," when this travel advice is updated."]},{"k":"p","s":["You can also ",["contact FCDO online","https://www.contact.service.csd.fcdo.gov.uk/posts/mozambique/british-high-commission-maputo"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["Help abroad in an emergency"]},{"k":"p","s":["If you’re in Mozambique and you need emergency help from the UK government, contact the ",["British High Commission in Maputo","https://www.gov.uk/world/organisations/british-high-commission-maputo/office/british-high-commission-maputo"],"."]},{"k":"hs","s":["FCDO in London"]},{"k":"p","s":["You can call FCDO in London if you need urgent help because something has happened to a friend or relative abroad."]},{"k":"p","s":["Telephone: 020 7008 5000 (24 hours)"]},{"k":"p","s":[["Find out about call charges","https://www.gov.uk/call-charges"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Risk information for British companies"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Overseas Business Risk service offers ",["information and advice for British companies operating in Mozambique","https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/overseas-business-risk-mozambique"]," on how to manage political, economic, and business security-related risks."]}],"chars":20441,"change":"New information about requirement for Electronic Travel Authorisation (ETA) ('Entry requirements' page)."},"https://theconversation.com/the-mecca-alliance-meets-the-red-sea-saudi-arabias-new-defense-pact-faces-its-first-major-test-292975":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"69e7dfc8e80a4ccb8426319508199c769c10b6ec3eb21e752666b698403f7515","read":"https://theconversation.com/the-mecca-alliance-meets-the-red-sea-saudi-arabias-new-defense-pact-faces-its-first-major-test-292975","bytes":189350,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"The Mecca alliance meets the Red Sea – Saudi Arabia’s new defense pact faces its first major test","by":[{"n":"John Calabrese","r":"Assistant Professor of International Relations, American University"}],"pub":"2026-09-29T12:42:58Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["When Saudi Arabia, Turkey and Pakistan ",["agreed to a mutual defense pact","https://arabcenterdc.org/resource/diversification-without-substitution-what-the-mecca-joint-defense-agreement-offers-saudi-arabia/"]," in August, it was principally seen as a political commitment. The “Mecca alliance,” as it was dubbed, stipulated that an armed attack on one would be treated as an attack on all three, accompanied by deeper military cooperation."]},{"k":"p","s":["That pact is no longer simply a promise on paper. Within weeks, the three governments began building out the institutions and military mechanisms needed to give that commitment practical meaning."]},{"k":"p","s":["With Houthi attacks continuing to threaten Saudi territory and Red Sea infrastructure, Turkey on Sept. 19 said it was prepared ",["to meet Saudi Arabia’s military needs under the pact","https://www.al-monitor.com/originals/2026/09/turkey-says-it-could-help-meet-saudi-military-needs-under-defence-pact"],". Four days later, Pakistan ",["appointed the first secretary-general","https://saudigazette.com.sa/article/664816/world/pakistan-appoints-first-secretary-general-of-makkah-joint-defense-agreement"]," to the three-country arrangement – officially called the Mecca Joint Defense Agreement."]},{"k":"p","s":["Then on Sept. 25, the Saudi, Turkish and Pakistani foreign ministers ",["convened on the sidelines of the U.N. General Assembly","https://www.dawn.com/news/2032546/pakistani-saudi-turkish-military-chiefs-meet-to-discuss-ways-to-assist-riyadh-under-makkah-defence-pact"],", reviewed progress toward institutionalizing the agreement, and called for an urgent meeting of their military chiefs. Those chiefs ",["met in Riyadh that same day","https://sana.sy/en/politics/2346036/"]," to discuss intelligence sharing, military coordination and the integration of capabilities."]},{"k":"p","s":["Far from diplomatic and security humdrum, these developments make the Mecca pact about more than territorial defense in a region beset by myriad challenges and conflicts, ",["from Iran","https://theconversation.com/topics/us-iran-conflict-73960"]," ",["to Yemen","https://theconversation.com/houthi-advance-boosts-irans-leverage-over-the-us-and-saudi-arabia-but-may-cost-rebel-group-its-legitimacy-back-in-yemen-291930"],". For Saudi Arabia, which played the leading role in bringing the pact together, the arrangement responds to a pressing strategic need: strengthening the kingdom’s capacity to deter threats to its territory and the Red Sea corridor while reducing its reliance on external security guarantees. Indeed, protecting the kingdom increasingly means safeguarding not only its territory and airspace, but also the maritime corridors through which its economy reaches global markets."]},{"k":"h","s":["From territorial defense to corridor security"]},{"k":"p","s":["The Mecca agreement emerged as Saudi Arabia and other Gulf states faced intensified missile and drone threats linked to the Iran conflict and ",["Houthi attacks","https://theconversation.com/rapid-houthi-advances-in-yemen-pose-massive-strategic-risks-for-saudi-arabia-in-the-gulf-292070"]," emanating from Yemen."]},{"k":"p","s":["But defending Saudi Arabia’s territory is only part of the problem. During the current crisis with Iran, Saudi Arabia ",["had to rely more heavily","https://theconversation.com/a-new-houthi-front-and-expanded-iranian-attacks-risk-sinking-gulf-nations-choke-point-workaround-and-widening-shipping-risks-288218"]," on its western coast and the Red Sea as an alternative outlet for energy exports after the Strait of Hormuz became severely constrained. The ",["East-West pipeline","https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/saudi-arabia-resumes-oil-exports-via-east-west-pipeline-after-repairs-sources-say-314c9ae8"]," carries Saudi crude across the kingdom to the port of Yanbu, allowing oil to reach the Red Sea without passing through Hormuz. Once that route becomes more important, however, the Bab el-Mandeb becomes a strategic vulnerability."]},{"k":"p","s":["This is where two developments that might otherwise appear unrelated begin to fit together. On July 30, Saudi Arabia and 13 other countries ",["announced a Multinational Maritime Defense Alliance","https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/7/30/saudi-arabia-announces-maritime-defence-alliance-to-secure-vital-waterways"]," to protect shipping through the Bab el-Mandeb, Red Sea and Gulf of Aden. Turkey and Pakistan, ",["members of that maritime coalition","https://wcys.org/saudi-led-coalition-of-14-nations-establishes-defensive-maritime-alliance-to-secure-bab-al-mandab-and-the-red-sea/"],", helped launch the Mecca pact just days later."]},{"k":"p","s":["The two arrangements address different parts of the same strategic problem. The Mecca pact provides a framework for territorial and air defense; the maritime coalition seeks to protect the sea-lanes through which Saudi Arabia’s economy increasingly depends on for moving energy and goods. The distinction between the two becomes less meaningful ",["when an attack on a Saudi pipeline","https://www.reuters.com/business/energy/saudi-arabia-restarts-east-west-oil-pipeline-resume-exports-yanbu-sources-say-2026-09-22/"],", port or tanker can have consequences for the same national security interests as an attack on Saudi airspace."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Houthi campaign illustrates the problem. Attacks originating in Yemen have demonstrated that Saudi Arabia’s vulnerability ",["cannot be confined","https://theconversation.com/rapid-houthi-advances-in-yemen-pose-massive-strategic-risks-for-saudi-arabia-in-the-gulf-292070"]," to its borders. A missile or drone aimed at ",["Saudi infrastructure","https://www.wsj.com/world/middle-east/yemens-houthi-militants-attack-saudi-energy-infrastructure-067fa4f7"]," and a maritime attack in the Red Sea may involve different weapons and operating environments, but both can disrupt the kingdom’s economic security."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Sept. 25 trilateral meeting therefore took place as the distinction between Saudi Arabia’s territorial and maritime vulnerabilities was becoming harder to maintain."]},{"k":"h","s":["Why Turkey is the connective tissue"]},{"k":"p","s":["Turkey sits at the intersection of these two security tracks."]},{"k":"p","s":["Saudi Arabia brings geography, financial resources and a direct stake in securing the Arabian Peninsula and Red Sea corridor. Pakistan brings long-standing defense ties with Riyadh and substantial military capabilities."]},{"k":"p","s":["But Turkey adds an increasingly sophisticated defense industry – ",["including drones and other systems","https://www.forbes.com/sites/pauliddon/2026/08/29/turkeys-homegrown-armed-drones-are-now-ubiquitous-in--the-arab-world/"]," – alongside a diplomatic and strategic presence stretching from the eastern Mediterranean to the Red Sea and Horn of Africa."]},{"k":"p","s":["That combination gives Ankara a potentially distinctive role. The Mecca pact needs countries with compatible capabilities, intelligence, coordination and equipment if its mutual-defense commitment is to be more than words. The maritime coalition faces a similar challenge in translating political support for freedom of navigation into a sustained security presence."]},{"k":"p","s":["Turkey is positioned to contribute to both."]},{"k":"p","s":["The two coalitions, however, remain distinct. Their memberships and mandates differ, and there is no indication of a joint command linking the Mecca pact to the broader maritime coalition. Nor does the September meeting of military chiefs establish that the three countries are preparing joint offensive operations against the Houthis."]},{"k":"p","s":["The emphasis so far has been on coordination, intelligence and capability integration."]},{"k":"p","s":["The significance therefore lies less in the emergence of a NATO-style regional alliance than in the possibility that separate defense initiatives are beginning to reinforce one another."]},{"k":"h","s":["Regional backup plans"]},{"k":"p","s":["The developments also need to be understood in relation to the United States."]},{"k":"p","s":["Saudi Arabia is not replacing its long-standing security relationship with Washington with an alliance involving Turkey and Pakistan. The Mecca pact does not require that outcome, and Saudi Arabia ",["continues to rely heavily","https://www.nytimes.com/2026/09/20/us/politics/trump-yemen-houthis-red-sea-iran.html"]," on American military capabilities, training, intelligence and security cooperation."]},{"k":"p","s":["But repeated regional crises have put that reliance under growing strain, prompting ",["Riyadh to hedge against the risks","https://www.foreignaffairs.com/middle-east/can-saudi-arabia-keep-hedging"]," of depending so heavily on U.S. security guarantees."]},{"k":"p","s":["What is changing is the number of actors involved in providing security around the kingdom and the extent to which Saudi Arabia is attempting to shape those arrangements. As such, the Mecca pact can be understood as an additional layer of regional security rather than a wholesale strategic realignment."]},{"k":"p","s":["Regional states have long depended on outside powers while seeking greater strategic autonomy. The current situation in and around the Persian Gulf reinforces that tension because the threats facing Saudi Arabia are increasingly difficult to separate into discrete categories."]},{"k":"p","s":["The same logic applies to the maritime coalition. A U.S. naval presence can protect shipping, but the creation of a regional coalition gives Saudi Arabia and its partners a mechanism through which they can assume more responsibility for the security of the waters on which their economies depend. It also gives Turkey and Pakistan a more institutionalized role in a security environment that extends beyond their immediate borders."]},{"k":"p","s":["Whether these developments amount to a new regional security architecture remains uncertain. The institutions are young, military commitments are still being defined, and the maritime coalition’s broad membership does not necessarily translate into a willingness to deploy forces."]},{"k":"p","s":["But the developments are significant because they point to a shift in how Saudi Arabia is addressing its security vulnerabilities. Missile defense, maritime security and energy infrastructure can no longer be treated as separate problems: Disruption in one part of the kingdom’s strategic geography can quickly affect the others."]}],"chars":7748},"https://theconversation.com/putin-hopes-hardship-will-force-ukrainians-to-sue-for-peace-polling-suggests-it-wont-work-294619":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-17T17:18Z","sha":"0ed4a56e58738d9557806f37c8710dfd127ac89da3ca0c48de415ae92ebc7adf","read":"https://theconversation.com/putin-hopes-hardship-will-force-ukrainians-to-sue-for-peace-polling-suggests-it-wont-work-294619","bytes":188217,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"Putin hopes hardship will force Ukrainians to sue for peace – polling suggests it won’t work","by":[{"n":"John O’Loughlin","r":"College Professor of Distinction in Geography and Fellow, Institute of Behavioral Science, University of Colorado Boulder"},{"n":"Gerard Toal","r":"Professor of Government and International Affairs, Virginia Tech"},{"n":"Sarah Wilson Sokhey","r":"Associate Professor of Political Science, University of Colorado Boulder"}],"pub":"2026-10-27T12:15:22Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["Vladimir Putin has a theory of victory in Ukraine."]},{"k":"p","s":["It’s not the Russian president’s first theory – that was a ",["quick, dayslong campaign","https://www.npr.org/2026/02/24/nx-s1-5721139/russia-ukraine-war"]," – nor his second or third, which involved different ",["land offensives in the east","https://www.vox.com/policy-and-politics/2022/5/12/23065144/russia-donbas-offensive-may-slow-flailing"]," that quickly petered out. Instead, Putin’s latest hypothesis is that the ",["relentless bombing of Ukrainian cities","https://www.kyivpost.com/post/88109"]," will impose ",["so much hardship on civilians","https://ua.news/en/world/rosiia-khoche-zalishiti-ukrayintsiv-bez-svitla-vodi-i-gazu-pered-zimoiu-el-pais"]," that they will concede to Russia’s war aims."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, as ",["experts on","https://www.colorado.edu/geography/john-oloughlin"]," ",["conflict and","https://spia.vt.edu/people/Faculty/toal.html"]," ",["public opinion","https://www.colorado.edu/polisci/people/faculty/sarah-wilson-sokhey"],", we believe there is a significant problem with this idea. Chiefly, ",["extensive academic research","https://cornellpress.cornell.edu/book/9780801471506/bombing-to-win"]," shows that airpower alone rarely achieves decisive political goals."]},{"k":"p","s":["Bombs terrorize civilians, but our survey findings in Ukraine suggest they don’t change war outcome preferences. Indeed, recent data shows that suffering from ",["power outages","https://ua.news/en/energetika/cherez-rosiiski-obstrili-znestrumlennia-zafiksuvali-u-shesti-oblastiakh-ukrayini"]," and wartime stress in Ukraine has no relationship to support for territorial concessions to Putin."]},{"k":"h","s":["Putin’s plan for destruction"]},{"k":"p","s":["The targeting of Ukraine infrastructure has been part of ",["Russia’s way of war","https://theconversation.com/crippling-civilian-infrastructure-has-long-been-part-of-russian-generals-playbook-putin-is-merely-expanding-that-approach-192226"]," since the invasion of February 2022."]},{"k":"p","s":["But since August 2026, Russia has ",["significantly stepped up its attacks","https://acleddata.com/monitor/ukraine-conflict-monitor"]," against Ukrainian power plants and grid systems, especially in Kyiv. And due to Ukrainian air defense shortages, ",["more of Moscow’s missiles and jet-powered drones","https://www.wral.com/news/ap/28371-jet-powered-drones-outpace-ukrainian-defenses-as-manufacturers-race-to-build-new-interceptors/"]," are finding their targets."]},{"k":"p","s":["Russia aims to degrade the quality of life of Ukrainians, depriving them of electricity, water and transportation, according to a recently ",["intercepted Russian military document","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/16/attacks-on-ukraine-power-plants-show-russia-has-given-up-on-military-victory"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["“Russia is trying to cause a blackout in Ukraine – right before winter,” said Ukrainian President ",["Volodymyr Zelenskyy","https://www.dw.com/en/russia-wants-blackout-in-ukraine-as-winter-comes-zelenskyy/a-79686703"],", adding: “Russia is trying to leave millions of our people without electricity and heating.”"]},{"k":"p","s":["The broader Russian aim appears to be to make the Ukrainian capital uninhabitable, imposing so much hardship that residents will either depart or revolt against continued war."]},{"k":"p","s":["In combination with ",["more aggressive Russian tactics","https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/sep/04/europe-weighs-solutions-to-curtail-russias-growing-hybrid-warfare"]," and ",["hard-right Ukraine skepticism","https://blogs.lse.ac.uk/europpblog/2026/03/16/europe-ukraine-support-far-right-russia-divisions/"]," in Europe, Putin calculates Ukraine ",["will eventually","https://wwnorton.com/books/9781324117018"]," be broken, isolated and defeated."]},{"k":"p","s":["The city destruction strategy is not a new method of warfare by the Russian state. Post-Soviet Russia first employed a version of it during the first Chechen war of the mid 1990s, when much of ",["the city of Grozny was reduced to rubble","https://www.npr.org/2022/03/12/1085861999/russias-wars-in-chechnya-offer-a-grim-warning-of-what-could-be-in-ukraine"],". The strategy was ",["later revived by Russian airplanes in Aleppo, Syria","https://www.rand.org/pubs/commentary/2022/03/russia-destroyed-grozny-and-aleppo-is-kyiv-next.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["But is there any evidence for Putin’s theory of victory? Polling suggests not. Along with the ",["Kyiv International Institute of Sociology","https://www.kiis.com.ua/?lang=eng"],", we polled a nationally representative sample of 1,801 Ukrainians from June 9-26, 2026."]},{"k":"p","s":["The survey used a computer-aided telephone questionnaire and the results shown were proportionately weighted to accurately portray the view of residents in the area controlled by the Ukrainian government in Kyiv. It was the latest in a series of such nationwide polls ",["we have conducted","https://theconversation.com/ukraine-most-people-refuse-to-compromise-on-territory-but-willingness-to-make-peace-depends-on-their-war-experiences-new-survey-185147"]," since December 2019."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ukraine’s war trauma"]},{"k":"p","s":["There is no question that the Ukrainian population has been ",["deeply traumatized","https://www.news-medical.net/news/20260929/War-shocks-Ukrainian-mental-health-with-widespread-trauma-and-PTSD.aspx"]," by the escalation of the war since 2022. We asked Ukrainians nine well-being questions, which enabled us to create a stress index computed from how often they have experienced psychological symptoms since February 2022."]},{"k":"p","s":["The results on the index reveal that nearly 1 in 4 Ukrainians suffer from high levels of stress characterized by concentration problems, depression, irritability, distrust, physical weakness and other physical problems. More than 40% of the respondents in the latest survey indicated that they experienced two indicators of stress – nervousness and anxiety – often or nearly always."]},{"k":"p","s":["Stress is also related to war exposures. Asked about experiences of violence, roughly 20% of respondents said that they or a family member were personally injured due to Russian attacks, and 20% have directly witnessed violence by Russian forces. Sixty-nine percent of Ukrainians have a family member or close friend who has died as a result of this war."]},{"k":"p","s":["Power outages have been rampant across the country over the past year, disrupting everyday life. Overall, 65% of Ukrainians reported losing utilities “often” or “very often.” Only 1.4% of Ukrainians report having never lost power since 2022, and just 9% say they rarely lost power."]},{"k":"p","s":["There are important regional differences, however. While 73% of residents in Kyiv report that they lost power “often” or “very often,” the corresponding figure for residents in the western region is 54%."]},{"k":"h","s":["The impact on war attitudes"]},{"k":"p","s":["While levels of stress are highly correlated with experiences of violence and a frequent loss of utilities, we examined whether this cumulative hardship affects preferences for a ceasefire. The survey asked whether the current front line should be accepted as a ceasefire line for the sake of peace."]},{"k":"p","s":["The Ukrainian government has ",["said it is willing to accept this position","https://www.kyivpost.com/post/88043"],", but it remains controversial as it concedes part of the country’s territory to Russia, even if only temporarily."]},{"k":"p","s":["Zelenskyy announced on Oct. 21, 2026, that ",["freezing the current line of fighting","https://www.foxnews.com/world/ukraines-zelenskyy-open-freezing-front-lines-ceasefire-russia"]," was an option for negotiating peace; the Russian government, for its part, still covets all of the Donbas region of Ukraine and more."]},{"k":"p","s":["Ukrainians are highly divided on accepting the current front line, with 39% of respondents in our latest survey indicating they would – with varying degrees of reluctance – be open to that possibility, compared to 38% who would not."]},{"k":"p","s":["Critically, experiencing violence first-hand appears not to shape Ukrainian willingness to tolerate the de facto partition of their country at the current front line. Further, neither those who are more stressed nor those who have experienced more frequent power outages are more likely to favor accepting the existing front line as a ceasefire line."]},{"k":"h","s":["Ukrainians not ready to concede"]},{"k":"p","s":["Our polling data from summer 2026 is affirmed by more recent polling by the Kyiv International Institute of Sociology that supports the argument that bombing will not make Ukrainians more accepting of conceding territory."]},{"k":"p","s":["In a survey fielded from Oct. 6-18, 61% of ",["Ukrainians rejected giving Russia full control of the Donbas region","https://www.kiis.com.ua/?lang=eng&cat=reports&id=1643&page=1"]," in return for a ceasefire and security guarantees. Indeed, the institute has asked this question in seven polls throughout 2026, and opposition to conceding Donbas has risen from 54% in January to 61% over the course of the year. Kyiv has been pummeled by Russian missiles and drones in recent weeks. But among all Ukrainian regions surveyed, Kyiv respondents had the lowest support for conceding the Donbas territory."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another question from the October 2026 survey asked how long respondents are willing to endure war: 62% chose the option “as long as necessary,” a 14-point increase from April this year and the same percent as December 2025. The figure at the outset of the war in May 2022 was only 9 points higher."]},{"k":"p","s":["We know that historical evidence does not predict the future. Nevertheless, our survey results suggest that increasing wartime hardship against Ukrainians will not coerce them into accepting territorial concessions."]},{"k":"p","s":["There is currently no persuasive survey evidence that bombing Ukrainians will succeed in making them capitulate to Russian demands. Ukrainians are stressed, war-weary and hungry for peace – but not on Russia’s terms."]}],"chars":7214},"https://theconversation.com/how-mark-carneys-russian-hockey-ban-tests-the-global-rule-book-296806":{"r":"conversation","at":"2026-11-23T16:35Z","sha":"37ed0f7774343a072b622622d1ac09845f2a00e0bfeebde27c447b0886a389af","read":"https://theconversation.com/how-mark-carneys-russian-hockey-ban-tests-the-global-rule-book-296806","bytes":183524,"x":"fulltext v1","title":"How Mark Carney’s Russian hockey ban tests the global rule book","by":[{"n":"Aaron Ettinger","r":"Associate Professor, International Relations, Carleton University"}],"pub":"2026-11-23T15:34:20Z","mod":"","blocks":[{"k":"p","s":["The ",["Court of Arbitration for Sport","https://www.tas-cas.org/generated/assets/lists/dceab111-07bc-435f-b5f9-de88eff9db72/CAS%20Media%20Release_12573%20et%20al_final.pdf"]," (CAS) recently rejected the collective shunning of Russian athletes in international hockey. In doing so, it created a geopolitical test of Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney’s key foreign policy tenets."]},{"k":"p","s":["The current exclusion of Russian teams stems from ",["Russia’s invasion of Ukraine in February 2022","https://theconversation.com/topics/ukraine-invasion-2022-117045"],". The International Ice Hockey Federation (IIHF), along with the International Olympic Committee and FIFA, ",["banned Russia and its ally, Belarus, from their competitions","https://theconversation.com/sports-are-political-reaction-and-inaction-to-putins-war-of-aggression-178115"]," as part of the wider global effort to penalize the Kremlin."]},{"k":"p","s":["The IIHF reiterated its position in early 2026, citing the safety and security of all participants and the “ ",["integrity of its competitions","https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7738497/2026/10/30/russia-hockey-cas-ban/"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":["In October, a three-member CAS tribunal found that unconvincing: there was insufficient evidence to establish the legal requirements for non-participation. Only substantiated security concerns could justify national exclusions. The CAS set aside the IIHF decision on procedural grounds and left it at that."]},{"k":"p","s":["Naturally, the Russian Ice Hockey Federation welcomed the decision and declared its ",["intention to participate","https://www.reuters.com/sports/cas-rules-that-russia-can-compete-world-championships-2026-10-30/"]," in the World Junior Championship in Alberta starting on Dec. 26."]},{"k":"h","s":["Banned by Canada"]},{"k":"p","s":["Hockey federations in Canada and Europe expressed ",["varying degrees of disappointment","https://www.instagram.com/p/DfIlEdqvyEE/"],", with some countries ",["threatening to boycott","https://www.espn.com/olympics/story/_/id/50368089/norway-pledges-boycott-hockey-worlds-russia"]," games against Russian players."]},{"k":"p","s":[["Germany is threatening to abdicate its hosting duties","https://sports.yahoo.com/articles/germany-mull-handing-back-ice-154834874.html"]," for the May 2027 Men’s World Championship if Russia participates. Carney called the return of Russian teams “ ",["unwelcome","https://www.politico.com/news/2026/10/30/ruling-allowing-russia-back-in-ice-hockey-tournaments-is-unwelcome-mark-carney-says"],"” and later said the ",["the Russian team would be barred from competing in Alberta for the World Juniors","https://www.cbc.ca/sports/hockey/iihf-world-juniors-russia-not-competing-9.7422880"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The IIHF has since made Russia’s exclusion from the December-January World Juniors complete by yielding to the Canadian government’s restrictions. Russian officials were apoplectic and the IIHF website was hit by ",["cyber attacks","https://www.sportsnet.ca/world-juniors/article/iihf-website-hit-by-apparent-hack-after-russia-excluded-from-world-juniors/"],". Notably, USA Hockey has been quiet."]},{"k":"h","s":["CAS decision and Canadian foreign policy"]},{"k":"p","s":["The CAS ruling and its fallout may be peripheral to what is known as ",["great power politics","https://theconversation.com/what-makes-great-powers-great-and-how-will-they-adapt-to-a-multipolar-world-260969"],", but it’s also a test of the post-rules-based global order."]},{"k":"p","s":["For Canada, the implications of disregarding the CAS ruling are considerable. For decades, ",["Canada’s foreign policy was premised on the legitimacy of international institutions and a commitment to multilateralism","https://www.cigionline.org/articles/canada-in-the-world-the-multilateralist-tradition-in-canadian-foreign-policy/"],". The CAS is one component of the interlocking machinery of that order."]},{"k":"p","s":["Now, major hockey countries like Canada find themselves on the horns of a dilemma: accept the CAS ruling and undermine the collective pressure campaign against Russia, or ignore the ruling and accelerate the erosion of yet another multilateral institution."]},{"k":"p","s":["Two or three years ago, Canada might have held its nose and accepted the CAS decision because of its procedural legitimacy. Trusting the global process was Canada’s overall strategy for decades but under Carney, that’s no longer the case."]},{"k":"p","s":["Yet, even in this ",["period of “rupture","https://www.weforum.org/stories/forum-in-focus/davos-2026-special-address-by-mark-carney-prime-minister-of-canada"],",” multilateral rules are still important. It’s not clear there’s any more wisdom in accelerating the old order’s demise than there is in practising what Carney has called “ ",["naïve multilateralism","https://www.cbc.ca/news/politics/carney-davos-speech-9.7052725"],".”"]},{"k":"p","s":["Read more: ",["Mark Carney’s Davos speech marks a major departure from Canada’s usual approach to the U.S.","https://theconversation.com/mark-carneys-davos-speech-marks-a-major-departure-from-canadas-usual-approach-to-the-u-s-274090"]]},{"k":"h","s":["Canada’s bad options"]},{"k":"p","s":["As host of the World Juniors, Canada was the first country with a decision to make — and future hosts are watching. Allowing the Russians to participate was likely never going to happen. Unfortunately, every option comes at a high cost."]},{"k":"p","s":["The easiest approach would have been to say it was too late to include Russia in the 2026 World Juniors. That would have eased pressure on the federal government and Hockey Canada, but it would have passed the buck to the ",["Czech Republic, hosts of the Under-18 Women’s World Championship in January 2027","https://thehockeynews.com/womens/international/czechia-set-to-host-2027-u-18-womens-world-championships-in-january"],". It also wouldn’t have been the type of middle power leadership that Canada has been trying to signal."]},{"k":"p","s":["Another half-measure would have been to allow Russia’s players to compete under a ",["neutral banner","https://www.cbc.ca/sports/olympics/ioc-ends-neutral-status-vetting-russia-2028-la-olympics-9.7261242"],", but that doesn’t fool anyone and has even been used by Russia’s propagandists as a ",["point of pride","https://www.nytimes.com/2021/08/01/world/europe/russia-ban-olympics.html"],"."]},{"k":"p","s":["The option Canada ultimately took is, ironically, right out of Donald Trump’s playbook: ignore the CAS decision and make up your own rules. Carney’s declaration that “Russians will not be there” means denying entry visas to players, coaches and staff, much like what the ",["American president did to Iran","https://www.cfr.org/articles/the-u-s-is-co-hosting-the-world-cup-but-much-of-the-world-cant-attend"]," prior to the 2026 FIFA World Cup."]},{"k":"p","s":["For Canada though, ignoring inconvenient rulings is vice masquerading as virtue."]},{"k":"h","s":["Back in from the cold?"]},{"k":"p","s":["Regardless of Canada’s decision, the integration of Russia into the sporting fold is ",["already underway","https://www.cbc.ca/sports/olympics/ioc-ends-neutral-status-vetting-russia-2028-la-olympics-9.7261242"]," in both the IOC and FIFA. The Court of Arbitration’s decision may serve as the basis for further reintegration — and Trump may accelerate the process."]},{"k":"p","s":["He’ll still be president when the United States hosts the Men’s Under-18 Hockey World Championship in April 2027 and the Summer Olympic Games in 2028. Trump’s pro-Russia tendencies may prompt him to strongarm the IIHF and IOC into bringing Russia back in from the cold."]},{"k":"p","s":["For now, the Carney government has leaned into the rupture. Ignoring the court ruling, blocking Russia’s participation and standing with Canada’s European allies is consistent with Carney’s new skepticism toward the aforementioned naive multilateralism."]},{"k":"p","s":["But it comes at a cost to whatever remains of the ",["rules-based international order","https://doi.org/10.1111/aspp.70034"],"."]}],"chars":5342}};
